Principles": "https://www.liquor.com/about-us-4782181#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT90M", "description": "Utilizing Indigenous American ingredients like fall and winter squash, maple syrup, and apple cider vinegar, this non-alcoholic drink from acclaimed restaurant Owamni by the Sioux Chef is easy to batch in large amounts, and can be enjoyed all year long.", "recipeYield": ["80", "80 servings"], "dateModified": "2023-12-08T15:52:42.257-05:00", "datePublished": "2023-12-08T15:52:42.257-05:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "4", "ratingValue": "4.3"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/dagwaagin-fall-squash-shrub-recipe-8413668", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/cocktail-and-other-recipes-4779343", "name": "Cocktail & Other Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/cocktail-type-4779426", "name": "Cocktail Type"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/nonalcoholic-drinks-4779418", "name": "Nonalcoholic"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["4\\u20135 whole fall squash, peeled, de-seeded and shredded (approx. 5 quarts by volume)", "2\\u20134 pieces fresh ginger, about 2 1/2 inches x 1 inch, peeled and shredded", "3 quarts maple syrup", "2 cups water", "2 tablespoons juniper or peppercorn", "4 sprigs mint, including stems and leaves", "5 cups apple cider vinegar", "Soda water, to top", "Garnish: mint sprig"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Clean the squash. Wipe off any dirt and rinse under cold water. Cut off the squash stems, then peel or remove thick skin with a kitchen knife. Scoop out the seeds and strings (seeds can be saved and planted or gifted to friends for their own gardens).", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Shred squash with a food processor or box grater. Repeat the process with the raw ginger.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Place squash, ginger, maple syrup, water, and juniper or peppercorn into a large pot. The squash should be nearly covered with liquid, just below the \\u201csquash line.\\u201d Mix the ingredients with a cooking spoon.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Bring mixture to a boil then lower to a simmer for 20\\u201330 minutes, until squash breaks down. Drier squash may require additional water throughout the cooking process, so pour in water as needed to maintain the squash line, until the ingredients are cooked through and no longer fibrous.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Cook mixture down until a loose syrup forms and it reduces to roughly one third its starting volume. Taste and adjust as you go, but do not over simmer to a candy-like stage.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Remove pot from heat. Add mint sprigs to a separate heat proof container. Using a fine mesh strainer or cheesecloth, strain hot syrup over the mint. Reserve or discard solids.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Let syrup and mint sit for a minimum of 20 minutes. For best results, move to the fridge after 1\\u20132 hours or let steep overnight.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "After steeping, strain mint from syrup; reserve for another use or discard. Add apple cider vinegar to syrup, then stir together.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Serve 2\\u20133 ounces of shrub over ice. Top with soda water, adjusting to taste. Garnish with additional mint sprig.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:33:42.516605+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:21:43.901798+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:51.938866+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (31396, 'https://www.liquor.com/recipes/smoke-on-the-water/', 'liquor', 'Smoke on the Water', 'Liquor.com', 'https://www.liquor.com/thmb/0je0XSZ3X5jwbrhttWTFcKG14m0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/smoke-on-the-water-720x720-primary-a7c6b92874914d2ab2c34972cf2a013e.jpg', '{"name": "Smoke on the Water", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.liquor.com/thmb/0je0XSZ3X5jwbrhttWTFcKG14m0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/smoke-on-the-water-720x720-primary-a7c6b92874914d2ab2c34972cf2a013e.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 720, "height": 720}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.liquor.com/liquor-com-5196141", "name": "Liquor.com", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "PT0M", "headline": "Smoke on the Water", "prepTime": "PT5M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "433 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "fiberContent": "0 g", "sugarContent": "14 g", "sodiumContent": "5 mg", "proteinContent": "0 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "16 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.liquor.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.liquor.com/thmb/0v9c3WJ13dxUhITL99kMYCMFNjM=/778x180/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Liquor_Schema_Logo-bcd957a10f6e48d5892e1b39c1580f44.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 778, "height": 180}, "name": "Liquor.com", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Liquor.com", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/liquor.com", "https://www.instagram.com/liquor", "https://www.pinterest.com/liquordotcom"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.liquor.com/about-us-4782181#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT5M", "description": "A burning sprig of rosemary gives this fruity mezcal Margarita variation a stunning visual display.", "recipeYield": ["1", "1"], "dateModified": "2022-06-05T19:49:16.649-04:00", "datePublished": "2016-12-19T15:42:15.000-05:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "9", "ratingValue": "4.1"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/recipes/smoke-on-the-water/", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/cocktail-and-other-recipes-4779343", "name": "Cocktail & Other Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/cocktail-by-spirit-4779438", "name": "By Spirit"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.liquor.com/tequila-and-mezcal-cocktails-4779429", "name": "Tequila & Mezcal Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["Rosemary sprig", "100-proof alcohol, for soaking", "1 1/2 ounces Banhez Mezcal Artesanal", "3/4 ounce Cointreau", "1 ounce watermelon juice, freshly pressed", "1/2 ounce hibiscus simple syrup*", "1/2 ounce lime juice, freshly squeezed", "Garnish: flaming rosemary sprig"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Soak a fresh rosemary sprig upside down with 100-proof alcohol for five minutes.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add the mezcal, Cointreau, watermelon juice, hibiscus simple syrup and lime juice to a shaker with ice, and shake until well-chilled.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Double-strain into a rocks glass over fresh ice.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Place the prepared sprig upright in the rocks glass, and light immediately before serving. Extinguish before drinking. *Hibiscus simple syrup: Combine 1 cup water with 1 cup sugar in a small saucepan, and bring to a boil. Take off the heat and add 1/2 cup of dried hibiscus flowers or four bags of hibiscus tea. Let steep for 10 minutes then strain into a glass jar with a lid. The syrup will keep for up to a month in the refrigerator.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:35:50.735264+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:21:56.786485+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:46.569254+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (34799, 'https://punchdrink.com/recipes/cape-cod-margarita/', 'punch', 'Cape Cod Margarita', 'Punch Staff', 'https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Article-Cape-Cod-Margarita-Recipe.jpg?w=800',  E'{"name": "Cape Cod Margarita", "@type": "Recipe", "image": "https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Article-Cape-Cod-Margarita-Recipe.jpg?w=800", "author": {"name": "Punch Staff", "@type": "Person"}, "@context": "http://schema.org", "keywords": "mezcal", "description": "For this mashup cocktail recipe, food and cocktail scientist Dave Arnold uses a technique called the \\u201cjuice shake.\\u201d", "recipeYield": "Serving: 1", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "bestRating": "5", "ratingCount": "16", "ratingValue": "2.875"}, "recipeIngredient": ["2 ounces unsweetened cranberry juice, frozen into two 1-ounce cubes", "1 ounce orange juice", "1 1/2 ounces Cointreau", "3/4 ounce mezcal, preferably Del Maguey Vida (tequila may be substituted, if preferred)", "7 drops 20% saline solution (1:5 salt to water; alternately, just add a pinch of salt)", "2 \\"hard ice\\" cubes (two 1-ounce cubes of frozen water)"], "recipeInstructions": "Shake all ingredients until the cubes dissolve. \\u201cYou\\u2019ll hear the cube break up, and it will almost all be gone,\\u201d Arnold notes.\\nPour into chilled coupe glass."}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:43:19.064431+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:23:07.929188+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:49.449826+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (34888, 'https://punchdrink.com/recipes/the-long-island-bars-dirty-martini/', 'punch', 'The Long Island Bar’s Dirty Martini', 'Punch Staff', 'https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Punch_mallory-heyer_thumbnails-r3-2.jpg',  E'{"name": "The Long Island Bar\\u2019s Dirty Martini", "@type": "Recipe", "image": "https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Punch_mallory-heyer_thumbnails-r3-2.jpg", "author": {"name": "Punch Staff", "@type": "Person"}, "@context": "http://schema.org", "keywords": "dirty martini, gin, Martini, vermouth", "description": "A dirty Martini cocktail recipe from The Long Island Bar, made with gin, vermouth and a homemade olive brine.", "recipeYield": "Serving: 1", "recipeCategory": ["Classics", "Savory", "Strong"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "bestRating": "5", "ratingCount": "20", "ratingValue": "3.55"}, "recipeIngredient": ["3 ounces London dry gin, preferably Fords or Hayman\\u2019s", "1/4 ounce dry vermouth, preferably Dolin Dry", "1/4 ounce (or more) dirty Martini olive brine (see Editor\\u2019s Note)"], "recipeInstructions": "Stir all ingredients with ice, until well-chilled and diluted.\\nStrain into a chilled cocktail coupe.\\nGarnish with 2 olives on a pick."}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:43:26.082515+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:23:09.170285+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:50.851921+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (34929, 'https://punchdrink.com/recipes/tigres-airmail/', 'punch', 'Tigre’s Airmail', 'Punch Staff', 'https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Article-2-Airmail-Cocktail-Recipe-Tigre-NYC.jpg?w=800',  E'{"name": "Tigre\\u2019s Airmail", "@type": "Recipe", "image": "https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Article-2-Airmail-Cocktail-Recipe-Tigre-NYC.jpg?w=800", "author": {"name": "Punch Staff", "@type": "Person"}, "@context": "http://schema.org", "keywords": "", "description": "This Airmail cocktail recipe from New York City bar Tigre combines a blend of rums, Champagne, lime and cane syrup.", "recipeYield": "Serving: 1", "recipeCategory": ["Classics", "Royale", "Citrusy"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "bestRating": "5", "ratingCount": "8", "ratingValue": "4.375"}, "recipeIngredient": ["1/2 ounce agricole rum, preferably Rhum J.M Terroir Volcanique agricole rum", "1/2 ounce aged rum, preferably Santa Teresa 1796 rum", "1/2 ounce lightly aged rum, preferably Probitas rum", "scant 1/2 ounce lime juice", "scant 1/2 ounce cane syrup (1:1, cane sugar to water)", "1/8 ounce (3/4 teaspoon) lime cordial (see Editor\\u2019s Note)", "Champagne, to top"], "recipeInstructions": "Add all ingredients except the Champagne to a tin.\\nAdd ice, and shake until chilled.\\nFine-strain into a chilled flute, and top with Champagne.\\nExpress a lime peel over the top, and discard."}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:43:29.044503+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:23:09.920571+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:52.298544+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (35014, 'https://punchdrink.com/recipes/swamp-thing/', 'punch', 'Swamp Thing', 'Punch Staff', 'https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Article2-Clarified-Swamp-Water-Night-on-Earth-LA-Cocktail-Recipe.jpg?w=800',  E'{"name": "Swamp Thing", "@type": "Recipe", "image": "https://punchdrink.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Article2-Clarified-Swamp-Water-Night-on-Earth-LA-Cocktail-Recipe.jpg?w=800", "author": {"name": "Punch Staff", "@type": "Person"}, "@context": "http://schema.org", "keywords": "", "description": "This clarified cocktail recipe turns the Swampwater, a green Chartreuse drink, into a milk punch with rum, lime, coconut and more.", "recipeYield": "Servings: about 35 to 40", "recipeCategory": "Fruity", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "bestRating": "5", "ratingCount": "3", "ratingValue": "4.3333333333333"}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 1/2 liters (51 ounces) green Chartreuse", "1 1/2 liters (51 ounces) pineapple juice", "1 1/2 liters (51 ounces) sencha tea concentrate (see Editor\\u2019s Note)", "750 milliliters (25 ounces) Cocchi Americano", "750 milliliters (25 ounces) clairin, such as Saint Benevolence", "500 milliliters (17 ounces) lime cordial (see Editor\\u2019s Note)", "375 milliliters (12 1/2 ounces) Planteray Stiggins\\u2019 Fancy Pineapple Rum", "375 milliliters (12 1/2 ounces) g\\u00e9n\\u00e9py", "1 1/4 liters (42 ounces) coconut milk"], "recipeInstructions": "Cover a slotted hotel pan with a dye-free piece of cloth and set it over a large, clear container.\\nIn a separate, nonreactive container, combine all ingredients except the coconut milk.\\nIn a third container, measure the coconut milk, then slowly pour the cocktail mixture into the coconut milk. Stir gently until solids form.\\nAfter the mixture separates, pour it over the cloth-lined hotel pan to start the straining process.\\nIf the milk punch doesn\\u2019t fully clarify after the first pass, pour the mixture back over the solids until the strained liquid comes out clear. (The milk solids are doing the work of clarification, not the cloth.)\\nRefrigerate the collected clarified liquid until ready to serve.\\nTo serve, pour 4 1/2 ounces of the mixture over a large ice cube in a rocks glass."}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:43:34.413333+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:23:11.409139+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:49.319864+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37122, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/coquito-spiced-coconut-drink-recipe-11872605', 'seriouseats', 'Coquito (Creamy Puerto Rican Spiced Coconut Drink)', 'María del Mar Cuadra', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/RA9k_Ky0wMa-aO5H2xBidHJ-9-A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20241220-SEA-Coquito-AmandaSuarez-02-66a603753db347b6a320abad21ed9529.jpg',  E'{"name": "Coquito (Creamy Puerto Rican Spiced Coconut Drink)", "@type": ["Recipe", "NewsArticle"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/RA9k_Ky0wMa-aO5H2xBidHJ-9-A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20241220-SEA-Coquito-AmandaSuarez-02-66a603753db347b6a320abad21ed9529.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/mar-a-del-mar-cuadra-5118873", "name": "Mar\\u00eda del Mar Cuadra", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Coquito (Creamy Puerto Rican Spiced Coconut Drink)", "keywords": "eggnog, puerto rico, rum", "prepTime": "PT180M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "282 kcal", "fatContent": "13 g", "servingSize": "Serves 8 to 10", "fiberContent": "0 g", "sugarContent": "29 g", "sodiumContent": "99 mg", "proteinContent": "7 g", "cholesterolContent": "25 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "31 g", "saturatedFatContent": "10 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT180M", "description": "Coquito is a Puerto Rican drink made from coconut milk and warm spices. Think of it like a Caribbean version of eggnog.", "recipeYield": "12", "dateModified": "2025-12-18T21:00:00.000-05:00", "datePublished": "2025-12-18T21:00:00.000-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["Caribbean"], "recipeCategory": ["Rum", "Beverage"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "1", "ratingValue": "5"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/coquito-spiced-coconut-drink-recipe-11872605", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/all-recipes-5117985", "name": "Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cocktail-recipes-5117858", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 (12 ounce) can evaporated milk", "8 cloves", "1\\u00a0(2-inch long) piece\\u00a0ginger, peeled and sliced crosswise into 1/4-inch thick rounds", "1 cinnamon stick", "1 (15 ounce) can sweetened condensed milk", "1 (13.5 ounce) can coconut milk (see notes)", "1/2 cup to 1 cup white rum (see notes)", "1/4 teaspoon ground cinnamon, plus additional for garnish", "4 large egg yolks", "1 teaspoon pure vanilla extract", "1/8 teaspoon freshly ground nutmeg, plus additional for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "In a small saucepan, bring evaporated milk, cloves, ginger, and cinnamon stick to boil over medium-high heat. Remove from heat and steep for 30 minutes. Strain, discarding solids. Cool to room temperature, about 20 minutes.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "In a blender, combine spiced evaporated milk, sweetened condensed milk, coconut milk, rum, egg yolks (if using), vanilla, ground cinnamon, and nutmeg in blender and blend until fully combined and foamy, 1 to 2 minutes. Transfer to bottles and refrigerate until chilled.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/QyBFr7nfs3yy9OPVsnyrHBtX90E=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20241220-SEA-coquito-AmandaSuarez-step2-ea52e3ac26f64fe1b24ca12d399cd182.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "Serve chilled, dusting with additional cinnamon and nutmeg if desired.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/5_9uVunPBneTg-piJOR5L38bdP8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20241220-SEA-Coquito-AmandaSuarez-01-e89141c79dde46709d7e3b4ece9e809b.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:09.402718+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:02.537992+00:00'::timestamptz, 'Coquito', 'alias', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:50.806838+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, '49fe4df91d9e444ac03930d91509f1b461c4d2c56c87e11359afece065400d4d', 'v1');
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37128, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/chocolate-mint-julep-cocktail-recipe-11734888', 'seriouseats', 'Chocolate Mint Julep Cocktail', 'Daniel Gritzer', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/4FeDqh_ycH-dFXjcRtYkMkQq_3s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2017__07__20170705-julep-variations-vicky-wasik-2-295a8dbe00ae4ba390f69d1bc2910b24.jpg',  E'{"name": "Chocolate Mint Julep Cocktail", "@type": ["Recipe", "NewsArticle"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/4FeDqh_ycH-dFXjcRtYkMkQq_3s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2017__07__20170705-julep-variations-vicky-wasik-2-295a8dbe00ae4ba390f69d1bc2910b24.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/daniel-gritzer-5118638", "name": "Daniel Gritzer", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Chocolate Mint Julep Cocktail", "keywords": "mint julep, mint julep recipe, mint julep cocktail", "prepTime": "PT5M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "69 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "servingSize": "Makes 1 cocktail", "fiberContent": "0 g", "sugarContent": "10 g", "sodiumContent": "3 mg", "proteinContent": "0 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "11 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT5M", "description": "This variation substitutes cr\\u00e8me de cacao for the sugar, adding a chocolate flavor that pairs well with both bourbon and mint.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2025-11-03T08:47:59.274-05:00", "datePublished": "2025-05-14T15:33:08.256-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["Southern"], "recipeCategory": ["Liqueur and Fortified Wines", "Whiskey", "Cocktail"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/chocolate-mint-julep-cocktail-recipe-11734888", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/all-recipes-5117985", "name": "Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cocktail-recipes-5117858", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["10 mint leaves, plus a generous bouquet of mint sprigs for garnish", "1 1/2 tablespoons (22ml) cr\\u00e8me de cacao, preferably Tempus Fugit or another high-quality brand", "2 ounces (60ml) bourbon or rye whiskey (see note)", "Crushed or shaved ice"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "In a julep cup or large rocks glass, gently muddle mint leaves until lightly bruised, then swab the glass&#39;s sides with the mint&#39;s aromatic oils. Add cr\\u00e8me de cacao and bourbon or rye and stir well. Half-fill glass with crushed ice and stir to combine. Fill glass completely with crushed ice and stir until outside of glass frosts. Add more crushed ice, heaping generously, then garnish with sprigs of fresh mint. Serve, adding a short straw if desired so that the fragrance of the mint bouquet will greet the drinker with each sip.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:08.112154+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:02.773304+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:50.108835+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37238, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/orange-atole-hot-mexican-corn-drink-orange-recipe', 'seriouseats', 'Orange Atole (Hot Mexican Corn Drink With Orange Zest) Recipe', 'Daniel Gritzer', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/WRr8GB8bWdyhAKTPkul3L931iIA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2015__02__20150202-mexican-atoles-drinks-vicky-wasik-29-c924d77304394027a1ca6b228879dcb4.jpg',  E'{"name": "Orange Atole (Hot Mexican Corn Drink With Orange Zest) Recipe", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/WRr8GB8bWdyhAKTPkul3L931iIA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2015__02__20150202-mexican-atoles-drinks-vicky-wasik-29-c924d77304394027a1ca6b228879dcb4.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/daniel-gritzer-5118638", "name": "Daniel Gritzer", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Ananonnie", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "@Erin R, atole is eaten for breakfast, often paired with tamales, so it''s a really nice addition to breakfast or brunch!"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "manhat", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Sounds like a relative of pudding. Also sounds really good for an evening snack. Breakfast I can certainly see, but I am really fond of my coffee then.\\n\\nWe are lucky to have several Latino markets here and I like going window shopping. I am just hoping that we get a couple of restaurants that feature real ethnic Mexican cooking."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Ananonnie", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "@Erin R, atole is eaten for breakfast, often accompanied by tamales. So it''s definitely a nice brunch addition. I was actually trying to decide on what sweet addition I wanted for tomorrow''s breakfast, and this post popped up and reminded me that this would be perfect."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Ananonnie", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Masa harina is ground nixtamalized corn. It has a different flavor from corn flour (as in very fine cornmeal, not cornflour which is cornstarch for Europeans). If you can find corn flour, odds are you can get masa harina. Do not confuse masa harina with masarepa, which is pre-cooked cornmeal."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "adgxv2000", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "So, what''s this masa harina exactly? Just regular corn flour? If yes, can''t I just use the corn flour available at the store? If no, what''s the difference?"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "PT10M", "headline": "Orange Atole (Hot Mexican Corn Drink With Orange Zest) Recipe", "keywords": "breakfast, citrus, corn, drink, winter", "prepTime": "PT5M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "73 kcal", "fatContent": "1 g", "servingSize": "serves 4 to 6", "fiberContent": "1 g", "sugarContent": "8 g", "sodiumContent": "77 mg", "proteinContent": "2 g", "cholesterolContent": "2 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "15 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT15M", "description": "Mexican atole, a hot drink made from corn, comes in a staggering variety of flavors, from sweet to savory, each one more delicious than the next. In this sweet one, the corn-flavored base, made from masa harina, is infused with orange zest for a warming, aromatic beverage that&#39;s perfect for winter.", "recipeYield": "6", "dateModified": "2025-04-03T19:07:41.091-04:00", "datePublished": "2015-02-06T02:35:00.000-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["Mexican"], "recipeCategory": ["Breakfast and Brunch", "Drinks", "Non-Alcoholic", "Beverage"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/orange-atole-hot-mexican-corn-drink-orange-recipe", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/all-recipes-5117985", "name": "Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/non-alcoholic-recipes-5117842", "name": "Non-Alcoholic Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1/2 cup masa harina para tortillas", "3 cups water, plus more as needed, divided (see note)", "1 cup milk", "3 (1-inch) strips orange zest from 1 large orange", "2 star anise pods (optional)", "3 tablespoons dark brown sugar (see note)", "Kosher salt", "Finely grated orange zest, for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "In a large saucepan, add masa and set over medium heat. Immediately add water in a slow, thin stream while whisking constantly to avoid lumps. Bring to a simmer and whisk in milk, orange zest strips, star anise (if using), brown sugar, and a generous pinch of salt.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/QL4e51ll325UCTAwtqiCI03FkXw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__images__2015__02__20150202-mexican-atoles-drinks-vicky-wasik-27-6ad62cba96b34e698f1b66f8dfb833d1.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "Return to a simmer and lower heat to low. Continue to simmer gently, whisking constantly, until drink is infused with the orange aroma, about 5 minutes. Discard orange zest strips and star anise pods. Thin with additional water, as needed, to create a thick-yet-drinkable hot beverage (the exact consistency is a matter of personal taste, see note), reheating as necessary. Taste, adding more sugar or salt if desired. Froth with a whisk or immersion blender, then ladle into mugs, garnish with grated orange zest and serve.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/9PazHfsOepouhlsjm2gPHAlLZQE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__images__2015__02__20150202-mexican-atoles-drinks-vicky-wasik-28-eb5a33de125b4db293f30003e5aac9b9.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:46.044963+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:06.128833+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:20.960757+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37303, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/frozen-jungle-bird-blended-rum-cocktail-campari-recipe', 'seriouseats', 'Frozen Jungle Bird Cocktail Recipe', 'Maggie Hoffman', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/5WtuAQn7WjEz67_g1w4bJP75wC8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2016__08__20160804-frozen-jungle-bird-vicky-wasik-1-9b4c16b1907b4c06929432e3d37d3290.jpg', '{"name": "Frozen Jungle Bird Cocktail Recipe", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/5WtuAQn7WjEz67_g1w4bJP75wC8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2016__08__20160804-frozen-jungle-bird-vicky-wasik-1-9b4c16b1907b4c06929432e3d37d3290.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/maggie-hoffman-5118865", "name": "Maggie Hoffman", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Frozen Jungle Bird Cocktail Recipe", "keywords": "campari, cocktail, frozen cocktail, rum", "prepTime": "PT10M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "277 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "servingSize": "Makes 2 cocktails", "fiberContent": "1 g", "sugarContent": "19 g", "sodiumContent": "6 mg", "proteinContent": "0 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "23 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": {"@type": "Duration", "maxValue": "PT610M", "minValue": "PT250M"}, "description": "Made with two types of rum and fresh pineapple juice, this drink, inspired by the version at Chicago&#39;s Three Dots and a Dash, balances deep, fruity richness with the bitter cut of Campari.", "recipeYield": "2", "dateModified": "2025-04-01T21:29:19.212-04:00", "datePublished": "2016-08-05T08:45:00.000-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Rum", "Cocktail"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/frozen-jungle-bird-blended-rum-cocktail-campari-recipe", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/all-recipes-5117985", "name": "Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/frozen-drink-recipes-5117844", "name": "Frozen Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["3 ounces (90ml) fresh pineapple juice (from about 1 1/2 cups or 200g fresh pineapple chunks; see note)", "1/2 ounce (15ml) Grade B maple syrup", "1 ounce (30ml) fresh juice from 1 to 2 limes", "1 1/2 ounces (45ml) Campari", "1 1/2 ounces (45ml) blackstrap rum (such as Cruzan)", "1 1/2 ounces (45ml) Navy-strength Jamaican rum (such as Smith &amp; Cross)", "8 standard ice cubes (about 160g)", "Pineapple leaves, for garnish (optional)"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Add pineapple juice, maple syrup, lime juice, Campari, blackstrap rum, and Navy-strength rum to a resealable container. Seal and freeze at least 4 and up to 10 hours.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "When ready to serve, pour chilled cocktail mixture into blender. Add 8 ice cubes and blend until uniform. Divide between 2 glasses. Serve immediately with pineapple-leaf garnish, if desired.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:47.555062+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:08.288239+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:56.571655+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37319, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/hot-spiked-cider-bourbon-caramel-popcorn', 'seriouseats', 'Hot Caramel-Popcorn Bourbon Apple Cider', 'Maggie Hoffman', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/G2Z0ALonk5GiKEpaVvMuCFBCzz0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2017__01__20170105-caramel-popcorn-hot-drink-vicky-wasik-2-830eaa81e4cd45c8b2f36b2f50470bc1.jpg',  E'{"name": "Hot Caramel-Popcorn Bourbon Apple Cider", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/G2Z0ALonk5GiKEpaVvMuCFBCzz0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2017__01__20170105-caramel-popcorn-hot-drink-vicky-wasik-2-830eaa81e4cd45c8b2f36b2f50470bc1.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/maggie-hoffman-5118865", "name": "Maggie Hoffman", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "kaveman", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "I''m not sure that this one we would <a href=\\"http://www.w3schools.com\\">eat</a> us"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "badseed1980", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "I think I want to try this with rye."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Rosie Redfield", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "This is the American meaning of ''apple cider'', right? Non-alcoholic non-clarified apple juice?"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "efish", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Where''s a recipe for Bourbon Apple Cider Caramel Popcorn? Because that''s what I want now. :)"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "staze", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Thanks @dann_the_caring_guy. Those are all good points. I''m also considering the nitrogen quick infuse options with the ISI Whip. I tried it last year with some herbs with so so results. Maybe it''s time for another try."}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "PT25M", "headline": "Hot Caramel-Popcorn Bourbon Apple Cider", "keywords": "bourbon, cider, cocktail, fall, hot drink, whiskey, winter", "prepTime": "PT5M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "94 kcal", "fatContent": "6 g", "servingSize": "Makes 1 drink, plus extra infused bourbon for another round", "fiberContent": "0 g", "sugarContent": "8 g", "sodiumContent": "52 mg", "proteinContent": "0 g", "cholesterolContent": "15 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "10 g", "saturatedFatContent": "4 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT30M", "description": "A caramel popcorn\\u2013enhanced spiked cider for a chilly day.", "recipeYield": "2", "dateModified": "2025-04-01T11:27:30.591-04:00", "datePublished": "2017-01-18T07:50:00.000-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Whiskey", "Cocktail"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/hot-spiked-cider-bourbon-caramel-popcorn", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cocktail-recipes-5117858", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/whiskey-recipes-5117847", "name": "Whiskey"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 cup caramel popcorn (1 ounce; 30g)", "1 cup (240ml) bourbon", "2 1/2 ounces (75ml) hot apple cider", "2 ounces (60ml) Caramel Popcorn\\u2013Infused Bourbon", "1 small pat butter"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "To Make the Caramel Popcorn\\u2013Infused Bourbon: Warm bourbon and caramel popcorn in a small saucepan over very low heat (you don&#39;t want it to boil much), stirring frequently, for 15 minutes. Strain through a fine-mesh strainer and discard popcorn. Infused bourbon can be kept in the fridge up to one week.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "For Each Drink, Microwave Method: Pour the cider into serving mug and warm until desired temperature, about 25-45 seconds, depending on the strength of your microwave. Add Caramel Popcorn\\u2013Infused Bourbon and stir. Top with pat of butter and serve immediately.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Stovetop Method: In a small saucepan, warm cider over low heat, about 5 minutes. Preheat serving mug by filling with boiling water, then discard water. Add hot cider and Caramel Popcorn-Infused Bourbon to mug and stir. Top with pat of butter and serve immediately.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:48.174111+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:08.764221+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:01.011669+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37401, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/cranberry-in-a-can-batched-rye-cranberry-drink', 'seriouseats', 'Cranberry in a Can (Batched Rye-Cranberry Shrub Cocktail) Recipe', 'Maggie Hoffman', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/h-TfMKkT7oY-HsQ4JiNufNgg7ko=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2017__11__HOFF_OneBottleCocktail_Cranberry-in-a-Can-edit-c500281219064eb984adcd4ee65238fc.jpg',  E'{"name": "Cranberry in a Can (Batched Rye-Cranberry Shrub Cocktail) Recipe", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/h-TfMKkT7oY-HsQ4JiNufNgg7ko=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2017__11__HOFF_OneBottleCocktail_Cranberry-in-a-Can-edit-c500281219064eb984adcd4ee65238fc.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/maggie-hoffman-5118865", "name": "Maggie Hoffman", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "PT40M", "headline": "Cranberry in a Can (Batched Rye-Cranberry Shrub Cocktail) Recipe", "keywords": "Christmas, cinnamon, cocktail, drink, easy, holiday, rye, whiskey", "prepTime": "PT5M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "2569 kcal", "fatContent": "1 g", "servingSize": "Makes 12 drinks", "fiberContent": "4 g", "sugarContent": "247 g", "sodiumContent": "40 mg", "proteinContent": "2 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "257 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": {"@type": "Duration", "maxValue": "PT10125M", "minValue": "PT105M"}, "description": "This warming and festive single-spirit drink recipe is perfect for wintertime entertaining: Make the easy cinnamon-spiced cranberry mixer far ahead of the last-minute chaos, add booze, and offer the drink in a pitcher for guests to serve themselves.", "recipeYield": "12 drinks", "dateModified": "2025-03-26T17:33:54.215-04:00", "datePublished": "2017-12-04T07:50:00.000-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Whiskey", "Beverage"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cranberry-in-a-can-batched-rye-cranberry-drink", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cocktail-recipes-5117858", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/whiskey-recipes-5117847", "name": "Whiskey"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 cup sugar (7 ounces; 200g)", "4 ounces (120ml) unsweetened 100% cranberry juice", "4 ounces (120ml) champagne vinegar", "5 cinnamon sticks", "24 ounces (720ml) rye whiskey (see note)", "12 ounces (180ml) Quick Cranberry-Cinnamon Shrub", "Garnish: 12 cinnamon sticks (optional), 12 fresh mint springs, 35 fresh cranberries or red currants"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "For the Quick Shrub: Combine sugar, cranberry juice, and vinegar in a small saucepan over medium-high heat and stir well to mix. Break up cinnamon sticks and add to the syrup. Stir constantly for about 5 minutes to dissolve sugar and bring mixture to a bare simmer, then remove from heat and let sit, covered, for 30 minutes. Strain through a fine-mesh strainer set over a resealable container and discard cinnamon sticks. Refrigerate shrub for at least 1 hour and up to 1 week.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "For the Pitcher Cocktail: Combine rye and 12 ounces shrub together in a 1 1/2\\u2013 or 2-quart pitcher and stir well to mix. Pour about 3 ounces (90ml) into each julep cup or rocks glass. Fill with crushed ice. Garnish each glass with a mint sprig (and cinnamon stick, if desired) plus 3 cranberries or red currants, and a straw.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:55.144546+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:11.113054+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:51.938866+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37429, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/guns-of-barbaresco-ava-genes-cocktail-apple-brandy-chinato-recipe', 'seriouseats', 'Guns of Barbaresco Recipe', 'Maggie Hoffman', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/DOoXxMxv0g9Ijbwk0dTOjsxmBL8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2016__03__20160310-chinato-cocktail-guns-of-barbaresco-vicky-wasik-1586e032c38c46a09294078d8b90529b.jpg', '{"name": "Guns of Barbaresco Recipe", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/DOoXxMxv0g9Ijbwk0dTOjsxmBL8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2016__03__20160310-chinato-cocktail-guns-of-barbaresco-vicky-wasik-1586e032c38c46a09294078d8b90529b.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/maggie-hoffman-5118865", "name": "Maggie Hoffman", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "rogisem", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "You''re gonig to make me poor Maggie Hoffman"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "PT5M", "headline": "Guns of Barbaresco Recipe", "keywords": "apple brandy, barolo chinato, brandy, cocktail", "prepTime": "PT5M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "285 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "servingSize": "Makes 1 cocktail", "fiberContent": "2 g", "sugarContent": "18 g", "sodiumContent": "14 mg", "proteinContent": "0 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "27 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT15M", "description": "This cocktail softens potent 100-proof apple brandy with bright lemon and Barolo Chinato, a bittersweet, herb- and spice-dosed digestivo made from one of Italy&#39;s best wines. The results are rich, fruity, and spirituous.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2025-03-24T18:04:26.729-04:00", "datePublished": "2016-03-14T08:10:00.000-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Brandy and Cognac", "Cocktail"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "1", "ratingValue": "5"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/guns-of-barbaresco-ava-genes-cocktail-apple-brandy-chinato-recipe", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cocktail-recipes-5117858", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/brandy-cognac-recipes-5117857", "name": "Brandy & Cognac"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 whole star anise pod", "1 1/2 ounces (45ml) straight apple brandy (100 proof)", "3/4 ounce (20ml) Barolo Chinato", "1/2 ounce (15ml) fresh lemon juice from 1 lemon", "1/2 ounce (15ml) strong Demerara syrup (see note)", "3 dashes Regans'' Orange Bitters"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Place star anise pod in a small skillet over medium heat and toast, stirring and flipping frequently, until fragrant, about 1 minute. Transfer to a plate and set aside to cool.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add apple brandy, Barolo Chinato, lemon juice, strong Demerara syrup, and orange bitters to a cocktail shaker and fill 2/3 full with ice. Shake until well chilled, about 15 seconds. Fine-strain into a cocktail coupe. Garnish with toasted star anise pod.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:44:57.487697+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:11.917725+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:59.279447+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37623, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/minnesota-goodbye-cranberry-french-75-variation-winter-cocktail-recipe', 'seriouseats', 'A Minnesota Good-Bye (Cranberry French 75) Recipe', 'Maggie Hoffman', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/vPtxRkht7KUcQf9qpq1SWQeXGUM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20231204-SEA-TwoBites-MinnesotaGoodbye-12-8e08d5c8453549549b06db0a48d80857.jpg', '{"name": "A Minnesota Good-Bye (Cranberry French 75) Recipe", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/vPtxRkht7KUcQf9qpq1SWQeXGUM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20231204-SEA-TwoBites-MinnesotaGoodbye-12-8e08d5c8453549549b06db0a48d80857.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "video": {"name": "How to Make a French 75", "@type": "VideoObject", "duration": "PT1M", "contentUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/aD3dWNKF-J6KJCfAt.mp4", "uploadDate": "2021-03-30T19:19:27.710-04:00", "description": "The French 75 is a refreshing combination of gin, lemon, and Champagne or sparkling wine. It''s bright and festive, perfect for the holidays, and an essential cocktail that everyone should know. Here''s how to make it. [Video: Serious Eats]", "thumbnailUrl": "https://cdn.jwplayer.com/v2/media/aD3dWNKF/poster.jpg?width=1280"}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/maggie-hoffman-5118865", "name": "Maggie Hoffman", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Danielle", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "This cocktail requires a bit more work (or a lot) than the average cocktail, at least in my house, but the effort is well worth it! The best holiday seasons include enjoying this and it&#x27;s easy to store and enjoy throughout the holiday season.", "reviewRating": {"@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "5"}}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Jeremy", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Made this for New Years-- quite good! Instead of making a large batch, we mixed the drinks one by one. Just replace the cups in the mix with ounces, and you''re good! The cordial is quite sweet. If you want a more dry cocktail, I would go with 3/4 oz. (or cup if you''re making the large batch) of the cordial and 1 3/4 oz./cup of the gin. For me, this gives a more balanced drink."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "MadPipps", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Have made this 2 years running. Boy what a great syrup. (Will second the mention that grapefruit is delicious but not required. Will mix well with most anything or even just water.)"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "CaliforniaFoodie962", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Delicious...We too have a family member that can''t have grapefruit juice so we substituted fresh squeezed orange juice. I also substituted vodka for the gin. Cocktail was a hit! On New Years Day we used just the plain cranberry compote in Champagne and it was a hit. Great recipe."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Rubymae", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "@arielgh33 - maybe blood orange juice?"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "PT15M", "headline": "A Minnesota Good-Bye (Cranberry French 75) Recipe", "keywords": "Christmas, cocktail, french 75, gin, holiday, new year, sparkling cocktail, sparkling wine, winter", "prepTime": "PT10M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "395 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "servingSize": "Makes 8 servings, plus extra syrup", "fiberContent": "2 g", "sugarContent": "53 g", "sodiumContent": "154 mg", "proteinContent": "1 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "65 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT145M", "description": "This drink, from Nathaniel Smith of Spoon and Stable in Minneapolis, hits all the right holiday notes: simmered tart cranberries, toasty spices, some piney gin, and a topper of bubbly. It&#39;s ideal for batching in advance of a party. The cranberry cordial can be made up to several weeks ahead, and the cocktail mix can be combined an hour or two before your guests arrive.", "recipeYield": "8", "dateModified": "2023-12-21T23:53:16.540-05:00", "datePublished": "2016-12-15T08:50:00.000-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Beer and Wine", "Champagne Cocktails", "Gin", "Cocktail"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "3", "ratingValue": "5"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/minnesota-goodbye-cranberry-french-75-variation-winter-cocktail-recipe", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-course-5117906", "name": "Recipes By Course"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/drink-recipes-5117861", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/cocktail-recipes-5117858", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/gin-recipes-5117855", "name": "Gin"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["3 cinnamon sticks, broken in half", "2 whole star anise pods", "5 cardamom pods", "3 whole cloves", "1 cup (240ml) water", "2 cups (400g) sugar", "Peel of one orange (use a vegetable peeler to remove zest only)", "2 cups (225g) fresh cranberries", "1 cup (240ml) fresh juice from about 8 limes", "3/4 teaspoon (3g) kosher salt", "1 cup (240ml) Spiced Cranberry Cordial (see note)", "1 cup (240ml) freshly squeezed juice from 2 pink grapefruits", "1 1/2 cups (360ml) London Dry gin", "1 bottle (750ml) chilled sparkling wine, to top", "Fresh cranberries threaded on cocktail picks, for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "For the Spiced Cranberry Cordial: Add cinnamon sticks, star anise, cardamom, and cloves to a saucepan and toast over medium heat, shaking pan frequently, until fragrant; make sure not to let them burn. Add water, sugar, orange peel, cranberries, lime juice, and salt and stir over medium-high heat until sugar dissolves. Bring to a simmer and cook, using a wooden spoon to smash fruit against side of pan, until all of the cranberries have popped. Remove from heat and let cool completely, 1 to 2 hours. Strain through a fine-mesh strainer into a resealable container. Cordial can be kept up to 3 weeks in the refrigerator.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/0Itseu_zsWOsLm2zyL3Gf35Xd8s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20231204-SEA-TwoBites-MinnesotaGoodbye-Step1-226d1f45ca7040c5a68e3ff5297294cb.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "For the Cocktail Mix: Up to 2 hours before serving, mix cordial, grapefruit juice, and gin in a pitcher, bottle, or resealable container. Use immediately or store up to 2 hours in the refrigerator. Cocktail mix makes 8 servings; feel free to double the recipe.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/u7VwzZW_KsF6KBeBl8AwDFtlTLI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20231204-SEA-TwoBites-MinnesotaGoodbye-step2-7df61fd3f9bc46c7a03d4d99ff6620e7.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "For Each Cocktail: Fill a Collins glass with ice and add 3 1/2 ounces (105ml) Cocktail Mix and 2 ounces (60ml) chilled sparkling wine. Stir gently and garnish with skewered cranberries.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/WF2ZufyUHOsJCUFRCgel201kOW8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/20231204-SEA-TwoBites-MinnesotaGoodbye-step3-28b6b75d8ec34678b2c9d21718172c1e.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:45:18.574801+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:17.929352+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:46.412664+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37683, 'https://www.seriouseats.com/fresh-lemon-syrup-recipe', 'seriouseats', 'Fresh Lemon Syrup Recipe', 'Stella Parks', 'https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/p4TdoMuvNmWStStvgOVbV5ECJ3o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2016__03__20160223-lemon-syrup-vicky-wasik-9-24d0003683df4724b285c251fcf73513.jpg',  E'{"name": "Fresh Lemon Syrup Recipe", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/p4TdoMuvNmWStStvgOVbV5ECJ3o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__recipes__images__2016__03__20160223-lemon-syrup-vicky-wasik-9-24d0003683df4724b285c251fcf73513.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/stella-parks-5119004", "name": "Stella Parks", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Pagh01", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "I''ve started collecting used lemons and limes in a big freezer bag, and when it gets close to full, I make this recipe. One useful trick - at the end of the process, I put all the rinds back into the bag, get most of the air out, and then use a rolling pin, a cast iron skillet, and my hands to squeeze the remaining liquid out of the rinds. I clip off a corner of the bag and squeeze the bag to drain it out the bottom. Much easier and less messy than a potato ricer.\\n\\nTwo pounds of rinds fills an old peanut butter jar, with a little bit left over."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Belle Couleur", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "GIRL!!!!! You were NOT KIDDING. This is like sunshine in a bottle and it is so useful! I have used it to give a kick to lemonade and cocktails, on crispy-fried fish as a sub for sweet and sour sauce and to make chinese restaurant style lemon chicken.\\n\\nI''m my granny''s child (waste not want not) so I froze the sugary skins. I used them to soak fruits for my Christmas (Caribbean style) fruit cake and minced a little to use in the actual cake instead of lemon essence. I dropped a few pieces in a chicken tagine dish and it worked beautifully. \\n\\nI''m going to try it with lime and grapefruit, and I will try salting the skins too, to see whether I get a syrup I can use instead of salt when seasoning fish (I will use the skins for roasting chicken). Also, I want to sugar some orange skins to see what that syrup comes out like. It should be nice whipped into cream to top bread pudding. I use orange peel when cooking smoked ham at Christmas and Easter and to make sorrel drinks, so I will have use for these too!\\n\\nSO excited!"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Schnuffichen", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "This worked beautifully. I wasn''t super organized about this, so I had to lemons (which were left over from Stella''s lemon bars recipe) hang in the fridge before I bothered to make the syrup (because clearly, it''s wayyyyy to much effort to simply put them in a bowl with some sugar). Then the rinds sat for something like 18 hours in the sugar. \\n\\nThe final product tastes amazing - just the right balance of sweet, sour, and bitter for my liking. Thanks so much! :)"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Kayt", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "It\\u2019s very similar to Korean Lemon Cheong. Also good with strawberries."}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Cathy C", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Every time we juice a lemon or lime, even if we zest it first, we save the rinds in a freezer bag in the freezer. After we have an entire gallon bag full, we mix it with sugar, about one part sugar to two parts fruit by weight, let it sit overnight, give it a few stirs, and strain it well. We don\\u2019t have a ricer, but we use a citrus juicer to the same effect. One gallon freezer bag of fruit yields about a quart of syrup and we usually freeze half. This stuff is amazing. Our favorite use is just to mix in with seltzer, but it\\u2019s great in cocktails and all the things mentioned in the article. This really is the perfect use for all our leftover rinds."}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Fresh Lemon Syrup Recipe", "keywords": "easy, gluten free, meyer lemon, no-cook, one bowl, syrup", "prepTime": "PT10M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "121 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "servingSize": "Makes about 8 ounces (1 scant cup; 230ml)", "fiberContent": "6 g", "sugarContent": "27 g", "sodiumContent": "3 mg", "proteinContent": "1 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "33 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/YfQU2tc6Ask4mMy6oMJDaulMqqE=/320x320/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Serious_Eats_Schema_Logo-30a63d9c07734d35836c8ff2d368419c.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 320, "height": 320}, "name": "Serious Eats", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Serious Eats", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/seriouseats", "https://www.instagram.com/seriouseats", "https://www.pinterest.com/seriouseats"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.seriouseats.com/about-us-5120006#toc-editorial-guidelines"}, "totalTime": "PT190M", "description": "Whether you&#39;re juicing standard supermarket lemons or their seasonal Meyer cousins, save the rinds for this vibrant yellow syrup. It&#39;s pure sunshine in a bottle, made from nothing but sugar dissolved by the acidic pulp\\u2014no cooking required! Since there&#39;s no added juice, it tastes more sweet than sour, but is balanced by the subtle bitterness of lemon oil.", "recipeYield": ["8", "1 cup"], "dateModified": "2019-02-05T10:58:59.000-05:00", "datePublished": "2016-03-24T04:45:00.000-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Cocktails", "Fruit Desserts", "Ingredient"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "8", "ratingValue": "4.9"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/fresh-lemon-syrup-recipe", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/all-recipes-5117985", "name": "Recipes"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/recipes-by-ingredient-recipes-5117749", "name": "Recipes By Ingredients"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/fruit-recipes-5117662", "name": "Fruit"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.seriouseats.com/lemon-recipes-5117649", "name": "Lemon"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["15 ounces (2 1/2 cups; 425g) \\"used\\" lemon rinds, from 6 medium lemons or 12 Meyer lemons (see note)", "7 ounces (1 cup; 200g) sugar"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Cut each lemon into a few chunks and toss with sugar in a large glass, ceramic, or stainless steel mixing bowl. Cover tightly and let stand at room temperature, stirring once every 45 minutes or so, until sugar has completely dissolved, about 3 hours (or up to 12 if timing is an issue).", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/BM4eKlLHosLxYIYoheHZkxO6mAk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__images__2016__03__20160223-lemon-syrup-vicky-wasik-collage-1-be6e6d2b1d2d4d50b25be6170b215e3d.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "Using a cheesecloth-lined or fine-mesh stainless steel strainer set over a nonreactive bowl, strain syrup. Working in batches, transfer rinds to a stainless steel potato ricer and squeeze to release any extra syrup, allowing it to pass through strainer into bowl; discard rinds. Refrigerate syrup for up to 3 months in a glass bottle or pint jar.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/thmb/S89CMMh4vowbG93qg95TqRSRmFI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/__opt__aboutcom__coeus__resources__content_migration__serious_eats__seriouseats.com__images__2016__03__20160223-lemon-syrup-vicky-wasik-7-b7e435ef850b4583beef456965333946.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 21:45:22.823597+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:19.879331+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:55.141598+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37834, 'https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/crushed-pineapple-and-mint-margarita', 'bonappetit', 'Crushed Pineapple and Mint Margarita', 'Cointreau', 'https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/60d37c3d03e0d4adf0b4cd86/16:9/w_2000,h_1125,c_limit/IMG_9897%20copy.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/crushed-pineapple-and-mint-margarita", "name": "Crushed Pineapple and Mint Margarita", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/60d37c3d03e0d4adf0b4cd86/16:9/w_2000,h_1125,c_limit/IMG_9897%20copy.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/60d37c3d03e0d4adf0b4cd86/4:3/w_2000,h_1500,c_limit/IMG_9897%20copy.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/60d37c3d03e0d4adf0b4cd86/1:1/w_2000,h_2000,c_limit/IMG_9897%20copy.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Cointreau", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.bonappetit.com/contributor/cointreau"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Crushed Pineapple and Mint Margarita", "isPartOf": {"name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "479px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "description": "BA''s Andy Baraghani mixes a crushed pinepple and mint margarita with Cointreau, blanco tequila, fresh lime juice, fresh pineapple juice, and mint #MargaritaSeason", "dateModified": "2021-06-23T15:50:23.426-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/60d37c3d03e0d4adf0b4cd86/1:1/w_2000,h_2000,c_limit/IMG_9897%20copy.jpg", "datePublished": "2021-06-23T15:50:23.426-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 5, "ratingValue": 3.2}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 oz. Cointreau", "2 oz. Blanco Tequila", "\\u00be oz. Fresh Lime Juice", "\\u00bd oz. Fresh Pineapple Juice", "1 Tablespoon Kosher Salt", "Lime Wedge, for Garnise", "1, 1-inch Piece of Fresh Pineapple", "Mint", "Ice"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Rub the rim of the glass with a lime wedge and reserve for serving. Dip the rim of the glass into the salt and fill with ice. Set aside.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Muddle the pineapple and mint in the bottom of the cocktail shaker. Add the Cointreau, lime juice, and tequila.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Fill shaker with ice, cover and shake vigorously until outside of shaker is very cold, about 30 seconds.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Strain the margarita through a fine-mesh strainer into prepared glass. Garnish with lime wedge.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "BA''s Andy Baraghani mixes a crushed pinepple and mint margarita with Cointreau, blanco tequila, fresh lime juice, fresh pineapple juice, and mint #MargaritaSeason", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:02:08.691511+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:24.205964+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:51.938866+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37850, 'https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/citrus-shandy', 'bonappetit', 'Citrus Shandy', 'Alex Delany', 'https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5ecd72f96de0d45497c35a4f/16:9/w_2000,h_1125,c_limit/Drinks-Shandy-Beer-Recipe-Lede.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/citrus-shandy", "name": "Citrus Shandy", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5ecd72f96de0d45497c35a4f/16:9/w_2000,h_1125,c_limit/Drinks-Shandy-Beer-Recipe-Lede.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5ecd72f96de0d45497c35a4f/4:3/w_1500,h_1125,c_limit/Drinks-Shandy-Beer-Recipe-Lede.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5ecd72f96de0d45497c35a4f/1:1/w_1125,h_1125,c_limit/Drinks-Shandy-Beer-Recipe-Lede.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Alex Delany", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.bonappetit.com/contributor/alex-delany"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Citrus Shandy", "isPartOf": {"name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "cold drink", "campari", "aleppo-style pepper", "orange", "summer", "quick", "easy", "drinks", "fourth of july", "memorial day", "labor day", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "479px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "Easy. Relaxing. Refreshing. Sunny. Filled with fruit and flavor. Yes, that describes your ideal summer, but also the shandy, the season\\u2019s most accessible cocktail. Keep a premixed batch of fresh juice and seasoning in your fridge to pour into a glass of light beer and ice whenever the sunny vibe needs to be turned up to 11.", "description": "Summer\\u2019s most accessible cocktail is much like the season itself: easy, relaxing, refreshing, sunny, and filled with fruit and flavor.", "recipeYield": "6-8 servings", "dateModified": "2020-06-02T04:00:00.000-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5ecd72f96de0d45497c35a4f/1:1/w_1125,h_1125,c_limit/Drinks-Shandy-Beer-Recipe-Lede.jpg", "datePublished": "2020-06-02T04:00:00.000-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 2, "ratingValue": 5}, "recipeIngredient": ["6 oz. Campari", "2 cup strained fresh orange juice", "\\u00bd cup fresh lime juice", "2 tsp. Aleppo-style pepper", "1 tsp. kosher salt", "4\\u20136 12-oz. bottles chilled light beer"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Vigorously stir Campari, orange juice, lime juice, Aleppo-style pepper, and salt in a large pitcher. Chill until ready to serve.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "To make 1 drink, pour about 8 oz. beer into an ice-filled glasses and add Campari mixture to your liking.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Do ahead: Campari mixture can be made 2 days ahead. Keep chilled.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Summer\\u2019s most accessible cocktail is much like the season itself: easy, relaxing, refreshing, sunny, and filled with fruit and flavor.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:02:11.705490+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:24.577070+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:50.108835+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37871, 'https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/spicy-grapefruit-shandy', 'bonappetit', 'Spicy Grapefruit Shandy', 'Amiel Stanek', 'https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5afd8ee50b5ec8242e7e1152/16:9/w_5232,h_2943,c_limit/50_dollar_brunch_12.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/spicy-grapefruit-shandy", "name": "Spicy Grapefruit Shandy", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5afd8ee50b5ec8242e7e1152/16:9/w_5232,h_2943,c_limit/50_dollar_brunch_12.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5afd8ee50b5ec8242e7e1152/4:3/w_3932,h_2949,c_limit/50_dollar_brunch_12.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5afd8ee50b5ec8242e7e1152/1:1/w_2950,h_2950,c_limit/50_dollar_brunch_12.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Amiel Stanek", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.bonappetit.com/contributor/amiel-stanek"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Spicy Grapefruit Shandy", "isPartOf": {"name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "cold drink", "british", "grapefruit", "quick", "easy", "drinks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "479px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "This sweet-tangy mixture transforms even the cheapest beer into a refreshing company-worthy cocktail, but even teetotalers (or, you know, the kind of people who don\\u2019t believe in hair-of-the-dog hangover cures) can enjoy a splash in a tall glass of seltzer.", "description": "This sweet-tangy grapefruit juice and ginger mixture transforms even the cheapest beer into a refreshing company-worthy cocktail, but it\\u2019s also quite delicious added to seltzer. ", "recipeYield": "10 servings", "dateModified": "2018-05-24T12:00:00.000-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/5afd8ee50b5ec8242e7e1152/1:1/w_2950,h_2950,c_limit/50_dollar_brunch_12.jpg", "datePublished": "2018-05-24T12:00:00.000-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 3, "ratingValue": 5}, "recipeIngredient": ["4 cups grapefruit juice, preferably fresh", "\\u00bc cup finely chopped pickled ginger", "\\u00bc cup (or more) pickled ginger juice", "Kosher salt, freshly ground pepper", "Beer, preferably light lager (for serving)"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Vigorously stir grapefruit juice, pickled ginger, pickled ginger juice, a small pinch of salt, and a good 20 cranks of pepper in a large pitcher. Taste and add more ginger juice, salt, and pepper if needed. Divide beer among ice-filled glasses and add a splash of grapefruit-ginger juice to taste.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Do Ahead: Grapefruit-ginger base can be made 1 day ahead. Chill.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "This sweet-tangy grapefruit juice and ginger mixture transforms even the cheapest beer into a refreshing company-worthy cocktail, but it\\u2019s also quite delicious added to seltzer.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:02:20.996191+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:25.061745+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:48.162306+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (37887, 'https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/barbados-gin-punch', 'bonappetit', 'Gin Punch with Lime and Mint', 'Nick Detrich', 'https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/596a5b4d6c75df51bc0b91f7/16:9/w_2734,h_1538,c_limit/barbados-gin-punch.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/barbados-gin-punch", "name": "Gin Punch with Lime and Mint", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/596a5b4d6c75df51bc0b91f7/16:9/w_2734,h_1538,c_limit/barbados-gin-punch.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/596a5b4d6c75df51bc0b91f7/4:3/w_2742,h_2057,c_limit/barbados-gin-punch.jpg", "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/596a5b4d6c75df51bc0b91f7/1:1/w_2742,h_2742,c_limit/barbados-gin-punch.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Nick Detrich", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.bonappetit.com/contributor/nick-detrich"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Gin Punch with Lime and Mint", "isPartOf": {"name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["punch", "cocktail", "caribbean", "coconut", "lime", "gin", "summer", "quick", "easy", "5 ingredients or fewer", "drinks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "479px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "Some coconut waters have a blush to them, so look for white or clear ones for making this punch recipe from bartender Nick Detrich of Cane & Table in New Orleans, LA. And yes, you can serve this in a punch bowl if you don''t have any coconut shells lying around!", "description": "Some coconut waters have a blush to them, so look for white or clear ones for making this punch recipe.", "recipeYield": "8\\u201312 servings", "dateModified": "2017-07-18T06:00:00.000-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.bonappetit.com/photos/596a5b4d6c75df51bc0b91f7/1:1/w_2742,h_2742,c_limit/barbados-gin-punch.jpg", "datePublished": "2017-07-18T06:00:00.000-04:00", "recipeIngredient": ["1 750-ml bottle dry gin (preferably J. Rieger & Co.)", "6 cups coconut water", "\\u00be cup fresh lime juice", "\\u00be cup (or more) sugar", "\\u00bc cup dry cura\\u00e7ao liqueur (preferably Pierre Ferrand)", "8\\u201312 coconut shells (optional)", "Mint sprigs and lime wedges (for serving)"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Whisk gin, coconut water, lime juice, sugar, and cura\\u00e7ao in a large bowl until sugar is dissolved. Taste and add more sugar, if desired. Chill until cold, at least 1 hour and up to 4 hours.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "If serving punch in coconut shells, use a hacksaw or cleaver to cut 2\\" off the tops: Working one at a time, saw part of the way through as you rotate the shell, or use the back of the cleaver to whack as you rotate. Keep working your way around the shell until it cracks open. You won\\u2019t get a perfectly smooth cut and that\\u2019s okay.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Ladle punch into ice-filled coconut shells or rocks glasses and garnish each with a mint sprig and a lime wedge.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Some coconut waters have a blush to them, so look for white or clear ones for making this punch recipe.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:02:19.381222+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:25.416074+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:56.571655+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38193, 'https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/bourbon-cherry-old-fashioned', 'bonappetit', 'Bourbon-Cherry Old Fashioned', 'Bon Appétit Test Kitchen', '/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png',  E'{"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/bourbon-cherry-old-fashioned", "name": "Bourbon-Cherry Old Fashioned", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png"], "author": [{"name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit Test Kitchen", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.bonappetit.com/contributor/bon-app\\u00e9tit test kitchen"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Bourbon-Cherry Old Fashioned", "isPartOf": {"name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "bourbon", "cherry", "orange", "drinks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/verso/static/bonappetit-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "479px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Bon App\\u00e9tit", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "description": "Bourbon-Cherry Old Fashioned Recipe", "recipeYield": "Makes 1  Servings", "dateModified": "2011-05-12T20:00:00.000-04:00", "datePublished": "2011-05-12T20:00:00.000-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 17, "ratingValue": 3}, "recipeIngredient": ["3 cherries from Muddled Cherry Syrup, plus 1 for garnish", "2'' strip of orange peel (pith removed)", "1/4 cup bourbon", "1 tablespoon Muddled Cherry Syrup", "1 dash orange bitters", "Orange twist"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Using a muddler or the handle of a wooden spoon, smash cherries and orange peel in a cocktail shaker until cherries are well mashed.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add bourbon, cherry syrup, and orange bitters. Fill with ice and shake vigorously 10 times. Strain into a Martini glass. Garnish with a cherry from the syrup and an orange twist.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Bourbon-Cherry Old Fashioned Recipe", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:03:35.035304+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:32.021766+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:48.728621+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38274, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/bellini-cocktail', 'epicurious', 'Bellini', 'The Epicurious Test Kitchen', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6585b41ed6bf94139b4fa298/16:9/w_6659,h_3746,c_limit/Bellini_RECIPE.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/bellini-cocktail", "name": "Bellini", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6585b41ed6bf94139b4fa298/16:9/w_6659,h_3746,c_limit/Bellini_RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6585b41ed6bf94139b4fa298/4:3/w_7090,h_5317,c_limit/Bellini_RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6585b41ed6bf94139b4fa298/1:1/w_5630,h_5630,c_limit/Bellini_RECIPE.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "The Epicurious Test Kitchen", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/the-epicurious test kitchen"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "5 minutes", "headline": "Bellini", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "pitcher drink", "prosecco", "italian", "peach", "beverages", "brunch", "nut free", "gluten free", "dairy free", "easy", "quick", "no-cook", "epicurious", "punch", "summer", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "totalTime": "1 hour 5 minutes", "articleBody": "Brunch would be nothing with bottomless mimosas, but real ones know the softer, subtler bellini is the true star of the breakfast cocktail bar. Many drinks historians believe the original peach bellini was created in 1945 at Harry\\u2019s Bar in Venice, Italy, by owner Giuseppe Cipriani. An innovator also credited with inventing carpaccio, Cipriani may have been riffing on the Italian tradition of marinating sliced peaches in wine when he concocted the cocktail recipe. Named for 15th-century Venetian artist Giovanni Bellini, the bubbly drink attracted generations of notable drinkers to Harry\\u2019s; in 2001, the Italian Ministry of Cultural Heritage made the bar a national landmark.\\nBut what is a bellini, exactly? A classic bellini recipe combines white peach pur\\u00e9e with a dry, fruity sparkling wine, usually chilled prosecco. It\\u2019s approachable and easy to scale up for a crowd, making it an ideal party punch.\\nShortcut versions that rely on peach schnapps or sweetened bottled peach juice can quickly become cloying. This version, adapted from the one served by Walter Bolzonella, current head bartender at the Hotel Cipriani, calls for fresh peaches blended into a smooth pur\\u00e9e. Many recipes add a few raspberries to the pur\\u00e9e for a rosy hue, but we like the pretty blush that comes from using ripe peaches only, with their skins left intact. If you want some contrast, drop one or two raspberries into the bottom of your glass; if not, garnish the drink with some extra peach slices.", "description": "The peach bellini cocktail combines bubbly prosecco with peach pur\\u00e9e. Learn how to make the brunch staple with this classic bellini recipe.", "recipeYield": "4\\u20136 servings", "dateModified": "2023-12-22T17:19:00.000-05:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6585b41ed6bf94139b4fa298/2:3/w_3752,h_5628,c_limit/Bellini_RECIPE.jpg", "datePublished": "2004-08-20T16:58:12.000-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 5, "ratingValue": 3.6}, "recipeIngredient": ["\\u00bd\\u2013\\u00be-lb. ripe white peaches, skin on, pitted and quartered", "\\u00bc cup lemon juice", "2 tsp. sugar", "1 (750-ml) bottle prosecco (preferably Nino Franco) or other dry sparkling wine, chilled", "Raspberries for garnish (optional)"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Blend \\u00bd \\u2013\\u00be-lb. ripe white peaches, skin on, pitted and quartered, \\u00bc cup freshly squeezed lemon juice, 2 tsp. sugar, and \\u00bd cup water in a blender on high speed until liquified. pour through fine-mesh strainer, pushing on solids. Discard solids; transfer pur\\u00e9e to a pitcher and chill until cold, about 1 hour.\\nDo ahead: Pur\\u00e9e can be made 12 hours ahead; keep chilled.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add one (750-ml) bottle prosecco or other dry sparkling wine, chilled, to pur\\u00e9e; stir gently to combine. Immediately pour into chilled white wine glasses or Champagne flutes. Garnish each glass with one or two raspberries (if using), and serve.\\nEditor\\u2019s note: This bellini recipe first appeared on Epicurious in August 2004. Head this way for more of our favorite brunch cocktail recipes \\u2192", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "The peach bellini cocktail combines bubbly prosecco with peach pur\\u00e9e. Learn how to make the brunch staple with this classic bellini recipe.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:24:54.651296+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:33.892356+00:00'::timestamptz, 'Bellini', 'alias', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:47.514183+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, '1a7b13cf9a64bd30f5d3c6f0566fdba8b134b5853a690d0736ec0dc0caefc4ef', 'v1');
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38285, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/bulletproof-rum-espresso-martini', 'epicurious', 'Bulletproof Rum Espresso Martini', 'Roger Kamholz', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/652dba1000b509e45fcc8ba0/16:9/w_5058,h_2845,c_limit/Bulletproof-Rum-Espresso-Martini_RECIPE.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/bulletproof-rum-espresso-martini", "name": "Bulletproof Rum Espresso Martini", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/652dba1000b509e45fcc8ba0/16:9/w_5058,h_2845,c_limit/Bulletproof-Rum-Espresso-Martini_RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/652dba1000b509e45fcc8ba0/4:3/w_5853,h_4390,c_limit/Bulletproof-Rum-Espresso-Martini_RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/652dba1000b509e45fcc8ba0/1:1/w_4390,h_4390,c_limit/Bulletproof-Rum-Espresso-Martini_RECIPE.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Roger Kamholz", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/roger-kamholz"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "10 minutes", "headline": "Bulletproof Rum Espresso Martini", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["epicurious", "martini", "espresso", "rum", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "totalTime": "20 minutes, plus overnight freezing", "articleBody": "It\\u2019s no passing coincidence that the meteoric revival of the espresso martini and the growing sophistication of coffee culture are happening simultaneously. There\\u2019s an exciting dialogue between the two trends, where the highly adaptable template of the classic Espresso Martini is serving as the sandbox in which cocktail and coffee nerds alike can play.\\nThe standard espresso martini build usually includes vodka, coffee liqueur, espresso, and simple syrup. Riffs on the drink tend to swap the base spirit, experiment with the growing roster of coffee liqueurs, use different coffee varieties, or all the above. This recipe exploits a hack that both bartenders and baristas would recognize: using fat to make a drink more velvety.\\nBulletproof coffee, a relative newcomer to the coffee drinker\\u2019s repertoire, uses butter to enhance the richness of your humble joe (supplements, usually MCT oil, are also sometimes added as a part of this wellness trend). Fat-washing is a popular method to make spirits more viscous and impart savory flavors; all it means is that the spirits are mixed with some source of fat\\u2014whether that\\u2019s bacon fat, sesame oil, coconut oil, or melted butter\\u2014and left to infuse in a freezer, where the fat will separate out and can be easily removed.\\nThis Bulletproof Rum Espresso Martini has a base of dark rum that\\u2019s fat-washed with vanilla-tinged brown butter. Rum and coffee are already longtime friends (see Kahl\\u00faa). The fat-washing process gives the drink an extra-velvety texture and amplifies the tropical notes that are tucked away in coffee.\\nYou can make this coffee cocktail with 1 oz. unsweetened cold brew concentrate, such as Grady\\u2019s, but the flavor will be less robust than if you use freshly brewed espresso. If you don\\u2019t have access to an espresso machine or stovetop moka pot, Cometeer\\u2019s frozen coffee capsules, thawed, make a great substitute.", "description": "Rum and velvety brown butter enhance this luxurious twist on the espresso martini. Get the recipe for this fun rum cocktail from Epicurious.", "recipeYield": "Makes 1", "dateModified": "2023-10-25T16:00:00.000-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/652dba1000b509e45fcc8ba0/4:6/w_2926,h_4389,c_limit/Bulletproof-Rum-Espresso-Martini_RECIPE.jpg", "datePublished": "2023-10-25T16:00:00.000-04:00", "recipeIngredient": ["4 Tbsp. (\\u00bd stick) unsalted butter, cut into cubes", "4 oz. dark rum (such as Myers\\u2019s or Goslings Black Seal)", "\\u00bd tsp. vanilla extract", "1\\u00bd oz. coffee liqueur (preferably Mr Black)", "1 oz. espresso, cooled", "1 oz. Fat-Washed Brown Butter Rum", "\\u00bd oz. simple syrup (1:1)", "Ground cinnamon (for serving)", "A coffee filter"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "To brown the butter, melt 4 Tbsp. (\\u00bd stick) unsalted butter, cut into cubes, in a small saucepan over medium-low heat. Let sizzle, stirring to prevent milk solids from sticking on bottom of pan, about 3 minutes. Cook, watching carefully and continuing to stir as solids begin to brown, until solids are a light chestnut brown and aromatic, about 4 minutes more; keep in mind butter will continue to darken off heat. Remove from heat and let cool, about 10 minutes.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add brown butter to a sealable freezer-safe container, such as a mason jar. Add 4 oz. dark rum and \\u00bd tsp. vanilla extract. Mix well and seal container. Freeze overnight, then pour through a coffee filter to filter out congealed solids.\\nDo Ahead: Fat-washed brown butter rum can be made 2 weeks ahead; cover and chill.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Combine 1\\u00bd oz. coffee liqueur, 1 oz. espresso, cooled, 1 oz. Fat-Washed Brown Butter Rum, and \\u00bd oz. simple syrup (1:1) in a cocktail shaker. Fill with ice and shake until well chilled, about 10 seconds. Strain into a chilled cocktail glass. Garnish with a sprinkle of ground cinnamon.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Rum and velvety brown butter enhance this luxurious twist on the espresso martini. Get the recipe for this fun rum cocktail from Epicurious.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:24:57.549358+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:34.118859+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:48.728621+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38320, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/caipirinha', 'epicurious', 'Caipirinha', 'The Epicurious Test Kitchen', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/643979cc6957537dfd61b47f/16:9/w_5987,h_3368,c_limit/Caipirinha_RECIPE_041223_51459.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/caipirinha", "name": "Caipirinha", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/643979cc6957537dfd61b47f/16:9/w_5987,h_3368,c_limit/Caipirinha_RECIPE_041223_51459.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/643979cc6957537dfd61b47f/4:3/w_4958,h_3718,c_limit/Caipirinha_RECIPE_041223_51459.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/643979cc6957537dfd61b47f/1:1/w_3808,h_3808,c_limit/Caipirinha_RECIPE_041223_51459.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "The Epicurious Test Kitchen", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/the-epicurious test kitchen"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "3 minutes", "headline": "Caipirinha", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "brazilian", "lime", "beverages", "dairy free", "gluten free", "nut free", "vegetarian", "vegan", "quick", "easy", "30 minutes or less", "5 ingredients or fewer", "epicurious", "alcohol", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "totalTime": "3 minutes", "articleBody": "Unlike many\\u00a0cocktail recipes that serve as rubrics for experimentation, a\\u00a0classic Caipirinha recipe requires precision\\u2014especially if it\\u2019s your\\u00a0first time making one. It might be tempting to simplify the\\u00a0Brazilian cocktail, which uses just three ingredients, by relying on bottled\\u00a0lime juice and\\u00a0simple syrup. Don\\u2019t do it.\\u00a0Muddling\\u00a0fresh lime wedges with crunchy sugar crystals gives this refreshing drink its signature texture and flavor; it\\u2019s even better if you do it directly in the glass you plan to serve it in. The\\u00a0pith and peel from those\\u00a0lime pieces provide distinctive character to the finished cocktail.\\nThe backbone of the drink is\\u00a0cacha\\u00e7a (such as Leblon or Avu\\u00e1). Called\\u00a0the national drink of Brazil,\\u00a0cacha\\u00e7a is a spirit made from fresh-pressed\\u00a0sugarcane juice. (Most rums, on the other hand, are derived from\\u00a0by-products of\\u00a0sugar cane production, such as molasses.) You can do all sorts of things with a\\u00a0bottle of cacha\\u00e7a, including swapping it in for\\u00a0tequila in a\\u00a0margarita or rum in a\\u00a0mojito or\\u00a0daiquiri. However, the\\u00a0Caipirinha drink is where this Brazilian spirit truly shines.\\nOnce your\\u00a0Caipirinha cocktail game is on point, there are a few worthwhile riffs to try. A\\u00a0Caipiroska swaps in vodka for the\\u00a0cacha\\u00e7a, while a\\u00a0Caipirissima uses rum. And if you have fresh passion fruit, try this variation.", "description": "The\\u00a0Caipirinha drink combines\\u00a0fresh lime and sugar with\\u00a0cacha\\u00e7a, a\\u00a0Brazilian spirit made from\\u00a0sugarcane juice. Learn how to make this classic\\u00a0cocktail recipe.", "recipeYield": "Makes 1", "dateModified": "2023-05-10T17:52:00.000-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/643979cc6957537dfd61b47f/3:2/w_6708,h_4472,c_limit/Caipirinha_RECIPE_041223_51459.jpg", "datePublished": "2004-08-20T00:00:00.000-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 5, "ratingValue": 4.8}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 lime", "2 tsp. sugar", "2\\u20132\\u00bd oz. cacha\\u00e7a"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Trim both ends off 1 lime and discard the ends; cut lime into wedges and transfer to a small highball or\\u00a0old-fashioned glass. Add\\u00a02 tsp. sugar and\\u00a0muddle it into the\\u00a0lime wedges. Pour in 2\\u20132\\u00bd oz\\u00a0cacha\\u00e7a and stir. Add\\u00a0crushed ice and stir well.\\u00a0\\n\\nEditor\\u2019s note: This recipe was first printed in August 2004. Head this way for more of our favorite summer cocktails \\u2192", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "The\\u00a0Caipirinha drink combines\\u00a0fresh lime and sugar with\\u00a0cacha\\u00e7a, a\\u00a0Brazilian spirit made from\\u00a0sugarcane juice. Learn how to make this classic\\u00a0cocktail recipe.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:25:09.369191+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:34.879689+00:00'::timestamptz, 'Caipirinha', 'alias', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:49.449826+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, '13a477ca524fe2f78c3109e147d65c3d36eb98261decdc6c0b2a1ebe6df89e4f', 'v1');
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38345, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/nonalcoholic-cucumber-spritz', 'epicurious', 'Cucumber Spritz', 'Jody Williams', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/641214d3b32e264851cd7e8a/16:9/w_5103,h_2870,c_limit/Bevanda%20al%20Cetriolo-RECIPE.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/nonalcoholic-cucumber-spritz", "name": "Cucumber Spritz", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/641214d3b32e264851cd7e8a/16:9/w_5103,h_2870,c_limit/Bevanda%20al%20Cetriolo-RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/641214d3b32e264851cd7e8a/4:3/w_5107,h_3830,c_limit/Bevanda%20al%20Cetriolo-RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/641214d3b32e264851cd7e8a/1:1/w_5107,h_5107,c_limit/Bevanda%20al%20Cetriolo-RECIPE.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Jody Williams", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/jody-williams"}, {"name": "Rita Sodi", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/rita-sodi"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Cucumber Spritz", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["nonalcoholic", "cookbooks", "cucumber", "lime", "cold drink", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "We opened a little bar called Pisellino across the street from Via Carota in 2019. It\\u2019s an homage to drinking all things Italian, inspired by our favorite caf\\u00e9s in Florence and Milan. We think that a fresh-squeezed juice and your latte macchiato should feel just as special as an evening cocktail. When we make this non-alcoholic beverage, the Bevanda al Cetriolo or Cucumber Spritz, we make a simple lime cordial for a dash of good old-fashioned bartending.\\nThis recipe was excerpted from ''Via Carota'' by Jody Williams and Rita Sodi with Anna Kovel. Buy the full book on Amazon.", "description": "A simple  lime cordial and a touch of salt make this non-alcoholic cocktail just as special as any boozy option. Make this cucumber spritz for happy hour.", "recipeYield": "Makes 2", "dateModified": "2023-03-16T15:11:58.635-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/641214d3b32e264851cd7e8a/3:2/w_5106,h_3404,c_limit/Bevanda%20al%20Cetriolo-RECIPE.jpg", "datePublished": "2023-03-16T15:11:58.635-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 1, "ratingValue": 5}, "recipeIngredient": ["6 juicy limes", "1\\u00bd cups (300 grams) sugar", "2 Tbsp. (20 grams) salt", "\\u00bc cup plus 2 tbsp. (90 ml) water", "1\\u00bd large cucumbers, about 1 pound", "3 ounces (90 ml) Lime Cordial", "4 dashes Saline Solution (about \\u215b teaspoon plus a few drops)", "1 Tbsp. (15 ml) lime juice, from 1 lime", "Ice", "Sparkling water or seltzer"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Peel the limes with a vegetable peeler. Toss the peels with the sugar in a bowl or a large jar. Using the handle of a wooden spoon or a muddler, bruise the peels a little to release their fragrant oils. Cover and leave overnight. The next day, juice the limes\\u2014you want to add 6 ounces (180 ml) lime juice\\u2014directly into the sugar and stir until it dissolves. Lime cordial can be refrigerated up to 2 weeks.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Stir salt and water together until salt dissolves completely. Pour into a small bottle, ideally one with a small opening, or a dropper.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Slice a few cucumber slices and set aside for garnish. Peel the remaining cucumber and pur\\u00e9e it in a blender or run it through a juicer. If blending it, strain the juice, pressing on the solids to extract as much as possible. You should have about \\u00bd cup juice.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Stir the lime cordial, saline solution, and lime juice together in a mixing glass (you will have 4 tablespoons of this base). Pour in the cucumber juice and stir well.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Fill two highball glasses with ice, pour the cucumber juice mixture into the glasses and top up with sparkling water or seltzer. Garnish with cucumber slices.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "A simple  lime cordial and a touch of salt make this non-alcoholic cocktail just as special as any boozy option. Make this cucumber spritz for happy hour.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:25:15.340950+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:35.414035+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:51.938866+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38393, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/su-cha-tibetan-butter-tea', 'epicurious', 'Su-Cha (Tibetan Butter Tea)', 'Julie Kleeman', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6232033f1e79b564b5f7e439/16:9/w_751,h_422,c_limit/Su%20Cha%20%E2%80%94%20RECIPE.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/su-cha-tibetan-butter-tea", "name": "Su-Cha (Tibetan Butter Tea)", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6232033f1e79b564b5f7e439/16:9/w_751,h_422,c_limit/Su%20Cha%20%E2%80%94%20RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6232033f1e79b564b5f7e439/4:3/w_751,h_563,c_limit/Su%20Cha%20%E2%80%94%20RECIPE.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6232033f1e79b564b5f7e439/1:1/w_751,h_751,c_limit/Su%20Cha%20%E2%80%94%20RECIPE.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Julie Kleeman", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/julie-kleeman"}, {"name": "Yeshi Jampa", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/yeshi-jampa"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Su-Cha (Tibetan Butter Tea)", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["hot drink", "black tea", "tibetan", "beverages", "gluten free", "vegetarian", "quick", "easy", "5 ingredients or fewer", "30 minutes or less", "simmer", "cookbooks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "Tibetan people drink yak butter tea in copious quantities throughout the day. More like a savory broth than a sweet tea, it is deliciously smooth and creamy when it is made using fresh butter. If the butter has become sour, however\\u2014as often happens in the more remote areas where refrigeration has not yet reached\\u2014it can taste very rancid. Such damage this has done to the reputation of what is a very fine drink!\\nIn Tibet, butter tea is made using black tea (often pu-erh), crumbled from a large brick (the tea was originally compressed in this way to withstand the rigors of the journey from China). For this version, we substitute brick tea with English breakfast tea bags and also add a little milk to match the creaminess of pure yak butter. A blender makes much faster work of the tea than a traditional wooden churn.", "description": "Tibetan people drink yak butter tea in copious quantities throughout the day. More like a savory broth than a sweet tea, it is deliciously smooth and creamy.", "recipeYield": "Serves 2", "dateModified": "2022-04-05T17:38:04.082-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6232033f1e79b564b5f7e439/3:2/w_750,h_500,c_limit/Su%20Cha%20%E2%80%94%20RECIPE.jpg", "datePublished": "2022-04-05T17:38:04.082-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 2, "ratingValue": 5}, "recipeIngredient": ["1\\u20132 English breakfast tea bags (we like Yorkshire tea), depending how strong you want it", "Pinch of salt", "2 Tbsp. (25 g) unsalted butter", "Scant \\u00bd cup (100 ml) whole milk"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Pour 1\\u2154 cups (400 ml) of water into a saucepan and bring to a boil over high heat.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "When the water is boiling, add the tea bag(s) and boil for a good 3\\u20134 minutes, stirring occasionally, then remove the tea bag(s) from the pan and discard.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Take off the heat and add the salt, butter, and milk, then use a hand-held blender to blend the tea until frothy. Gently reheat if needed, but do not bring back to a boil.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Tibetan people drink yak butter tea in copious quantities throughout the day. More like a savory broth than a sweet tea, it is deliciously smooth and creamy.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:25:20.623418+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:36.364144+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:49.319864+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38400, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/tamer-hindi-tamarind-beverage', 'epicurious', 'Tamer Hindi (Tamarind Drink)', 'Marlene Matar', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6239cb35fbeee9907e931cc8/16:9/w_845,h_475,c_limit/The%20Aleppo%20Cookbook_Tamer%20Hindi.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/tamer-hindi-tamarind-beverage", "name": "Tamer Hindi (Tamarind Drink)", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6239cb35fbeee9907e931cc8/16:9/w_845,h_475,c_limit/The%20Aleppo%20Cookbook_Tamer%20Hindi.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6239cb35fbeee9907e931cc8/4:3/w_858,h_644,c_limit/The%20Aleppo%20Cookbook_Tamer%20Hindi.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6239cb35fbeee9907e931cc8/1:1/w_862,h_862,c_limit/The%20Aleppo%20Cookbook_Tamer%20Hindi.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Marlene Matar", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/marlene-matar"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Tamer Hindi (Tamarind Drink)", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cold drink", "punch", "middle eastern", "tamarind", "beverages", "dairy free", "gluten free", "nut free", "vegetarian", "vegan", "nonalcoholic", "make ahead", "easy", "5 ingredients or fewer", "cookbooks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "This refreshing sweet and sour beverage\\u2014made with tamarind, water, and sugar\\u2014is popular during the month of Ramadan. The semi-dried tamarind paste used for tamer hindi can be purchased online or at Middle Eastern grocery stores.", "description": "Tamer hindi is a refreshing sweet and sour beverage\\u2014made with tamarind, water, and sugar\\u2014that''s popular during the month of Ramadan.", "recipeYield": "Makes about 10\\u00bd cups", "dateModified": "2022-03-23T11:48:54.924-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/6239cb35fbeee9907e931cc8/3:2/w_861,h_574,c_limit/The%20Aleppo%20Cookbook_Tamer%20Hindi.jpg", "datePublished": "2022-03-23T11:48:54.924-04:00", "recipeIngredient": ["12 oz. (350 g) block of semi-dried tamarind paste", "3 cups (700 ml) boiling water", "3 cups (1 lb. 5 oz. or 600 g) sugar"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Separate the tamarind mass into chunks and place in a bowl. Cover with the boiling water and set aside for a few hours until the pulp dissolves in the water.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Rub the tamarind pulp and seeds with your fingers, and add 3 cups (700 ml) cold water.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Place the mixture in a fine mesh strainer set over a large bowl and press on the tamarind to extract all the juice.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Transfer the pulp residue to a small bowl and add 2 cups (480 ml) cold water, rubbing the mixture with your fingers. Strain into the large bowl used above.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Repeat the procedure a third time with 1 cup (240 ml) water.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add the sugar to the tamarind juice in the large bowl and stir to dissolve.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Refrigerate and serve very cold with ice and water to dilute as desired (about \\u00bc cup or 60 ml water per 240 ml cup of juice).", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Tamer hindi is a refreshing sweet and sour beverage\\u2014made with tamarind, water, and sugar\\u2014that''s popular during the month of Ramadan.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:25:23.001942+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:36.521466+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:49.319864+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38404, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/old-cuban-cocktail', 'epicurious', 'Old Cuban', 'Adrienne Stillman', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/62042cf3483dece7f5eda34a/16:9/w_3743,h_2105,c_limit/old-cuban-andy-sewell.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/old-cuban-cocktail", "name": "Old Cuban", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/62042cf3483dece7f5eda34a/16:9/w_3743,h_2105,c_limit/old-cuban-andy-sewell.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/62042cf3483dece7f5eda34a/4:3/w_3751,h_2813,c_limit/old-cuban-andy-sewell.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/62042cf3483dece7f5eda34a/1:1/w_3754,h_3754,c_limit/old-cuban-andy-sewell.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Adrienne Stillman", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/adrienne-stillman"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "2 minutes", "headline": "Old Cuban", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "champagne", "rum", "lime", "mint", "beverages", "cookbooks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "totalTime": "2 minutes", "articleBody": "Audrey Saunders created this sparkly hybrid of a French 75 and a mojito at her bar, New York\\u2019s Pegu Club. Double-straining the drink (through a cocktail strainer and fine-mesh tea strainer) ensures that bits of mint don\\u2019t get into the glass.", "description": "Audrey Saunders created this French 75 and mojito hybrid at New York''s Pegu Club. Learn how to make the Old Cuban cocktail with rum and sparkling wine.", "recipeYield": "Makes 1 cocktail", "dateModified": "2022-02-09T16:10:48.765-05:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/62042cf3483dece7f5eda34a/3:2/w_3753,h_2502,c_limit/old-cuban-andy-sewell.jpg", "datePublished": "2022-02-09T16:10:48.765-05:00", "recipeIngredient": ["1 oz. (30 ml) aged rum", "\\u00bd oz. (15 ml) fresh lime juice", "\\u00bd oz. (1:1) simple syrup", "2 dashes Angostura bitters", "8\\u201310 mint leaves", "1\\u20132 oz. (30\\u201360 ml) brut-style Champagne or dry sparkling wine", "Mint leaf, to garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Combine rum, lime juice, simple syrup, bitters, and mint leaves in a cocktail shaker filled with ice. Shake vigorously for 15\\u201320 seconds, or until the shaker is frosted on the outside. Double strain into a coupe and top with sparkling wine. Garnish with a mint leaf.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Audrey Saunders created this French 75 and mojito hybrid at New York''s Pegu Club. Learn how to make the Old Cuban cocktail with rum and sparkling wine.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:25:23.916224+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:36.593582+00:00'::timestamptz, 'Old Cuban', 'alias', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:16.950432+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, '883ebbc9772303ef2147c833ea4cb794cacb4a068918d49bdc550b4d8e42a0ae', 'v1');
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38520, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/peak-season-slushies', 'epicurious', 'Peak-Season Slushies', 'Molly Baz', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5d377071c490cc0008d3b6f7/16:9/w_3145,h_1769,c_limit/peak-season-slushies-recipe-BA-062319.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/peak-season-slushies", "name": "Peak-Season Slushies", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5d377071c490cc0008d3b6f7/16:9/w_3145,h_1769,c_limit/peak-season-slushies-recipe-BA-062319.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5d377071c490cc0008d3b6f7/4:3/w_3001,h_2250,c_limit/peak-season-slushies-recipe-BA-062319.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5d377071c490cc0008d3b6f7/1:1/w_3414,h_3414,c_limit/peak-season-slushies-recipe-BA-062319.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Molly Baz", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/molly-baz"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Peak-Season Slushies", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cold drink", "smoothie", "mango", "pineapple", "watermelon", "honeydew", "lime", "beverages", "dairy free", "gluten free", "nut free", "raw", "vegan", "vegetarian", "nonalcoholic", "quick", "easy", "5 ingredients or fewer", "blender", "summer", "bon app\\u00e9tit", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "Think of this versatile fruit beverage as your base\\u2014then get creative. Try blending 2 tsp. mild red pepper flakes with mango, 1 Tbsp. finely grated peeled ginger with pineapple, or half a cucumber and some mint leaves with honeydew.", "description": "Think of this versatile fruit beverage as your base\\u2014then get creative. Try blending 2 tsp. mild red pepper flakes with mango, 1 Tbsp. finely grated peeled ginger with pineapple, or half a cucumber and some mint leaves with honeydew.", "recipeYield": "Makes 4", "dateModified": "2019-08-12T16:36:27.794-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5d377071c490cc0008d3b6f7/1:1/w_3414,h_3414,c_limit/peak-season-slushies-recipe-BA-062319.jpg", "datePublished": "2019-08-12T16:36:27.794-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 2, "ratingValue": 3}, "recipeIngredient": ["4 cups (1-inch pieces) fruit (such as mango, pineapple, watermelon, or honeydew), frozen", "3 Tbsp. fresh lime juice", "1/2 tsp. kosher salt", "2 Tbsp. (or more) agave nectar or 1 Tbsp. honey or pure maple syrup", "2\\u20133 cups coconut water or water"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Blend fruit, lime juice, salt, agave, 2 cups coconut water, and 2 cups ice in a blender on high, adding more coconut water as needed, until very smooth. Taste slushy and add more agave if desired. Divide among glasses.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Think of this versatile fruit beverage as your base\\u2014then get creative. Try blending 2 tsp. mild red pepper flakes with mango, 1 Tbsp. finely grated peeled ginger with pineapple, or half a cucumber and some mint leaves with honeydew.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:26:06.899591+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:39.095815+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:20.960757+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38559, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/cynar-spritz-cocktail', 'epicurious', 'Cynar Spritz Cocktail', 'Kat Boytsova', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5ac27180968b1f5f9f70b526/16:9/w_4000,h_2250,c_limit/cynar-spritz-cocktail-recipe-BA-032918.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/cynar-spritz", "name": "Cynar Spritz Cocktail", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5ac27180968b1f5f9f70b526/16:9/w_4000,h_2250,c_limit/cynar-spritz-cocktail-recipe-BA-032918.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5ac27180968b1f5f9f70b526/4:3/w_3556,h_2667,c_limit/cynar-spritz-cocktail-recipe-BA-032918.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5ac27180968b1f5f9f70b526/1:1/w_2667,h_2667,c_limit/cynar-spritz-cocktail-recipe-BA-032918.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Kat Boytsova", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/kat-boytsova"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Cynar Spritz Cocktail", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "aperitif", "spritz", "cynar", "prosecco", "grapefruit", "beverages", "easy", "quick", "bon app\\u00e9tit", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "Sweet, citrusy grapefruit pairs well with herbaceous Cynar, and adding dry Prosecco provides balance.", "description": "Sweet, citrusy grapefruit pairs well with herbaceous Cynar, and adding dry Prosecco provides balance.", "recipeYield": "Makes 1", "dateModified": "2018-04-20T09:00:00.000-04:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/5ac27180968b1f5f9f70b526/1:1/w_2667,h_2667,c_limit/cynar-spritz-cocktail-recipe-BA-032918.jpg", "datePublished": "2018-04-20T09:00:00.000-04:00", "recipeIngredient": ["2 oz. Cynar", "3 oz. Prosecco", "Splash of grapefruit soda", "1 (2x1-inch) strip grapefruit zest (for serving)"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Pour Cynar and Prosecco into a rocks glass filled with ice. Top off with soda, stir gently to combine, and garnish with grapefruit zest.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Sweet, citrusy grapefruit pairs well with herbaceous Cynar, and adding dry Prosecco provides balance.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:28:23.877065+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:39.841020+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:51.938866+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38594, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/fire-cider-tonic', 'epicurious', 'Homemade Fire Cider Tonic', 'Lukas Volger', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/58af3b41d011dc426027376b/16:9/w_1679,h_944,c_limit/Fire-Cider-hero-17022017.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/fire-cider-tonic", "name": "Homemade Fire Cider Tonic", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/58af3b41d011dc426027376b/16:9/w_1679,h_944,c_limit/Fire-Cider-hero-17022017.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/58af3b41d011dc426027376b/4:3/w_1500,h_1125,c_limit/Fire-Cider-hero-17022017.jpg", "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/58af3b41d011dc426027376b/1:1/w_1126,h_1126,c_limit/Fire-Cider-hero-17022017.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Lukas Volger", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/lukas-volger"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "20 minutes", "headline": "Homemade Fire Cider Tonic", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cold drink", "cocktail", "sauce", "horseradish", "garlic", "ginger", "beverages", "dairy free", "gluten free", "nut free", "vegetarian", "nonalcoholic", "pickle & preserve", "epicurious", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "totalTime": "20 minutes, plus 1 month", "articleBody": "While most recipes for fire cider use a heavy hand with the garlic because of its potent medicinal properties, we recommend going easy unless you want neighbors knocking on the door every time you crack open a bottle. Otherwise, you should feel free to tweak and embrace the flexible nature of this recipe. Fresh turmeric is a lovely substitute for dried\\u2014use about 3 tablespoons coarsely chopped or grated. And instead of dried hot chiles, use sliced fresh jalape\\u00f1o or habanero, or even smoke-dried ones. Consider adding other citrus, such as grapefruit or blood oranges, in place of or in addition to the lemon. Note: this recipe needs to sit for 1 month before enjoying.", "description": "While most recipes for fire cider use a heavy hand with the garlic because of its potent medicinal properties, we recommend going easy unless you want neighbors knocking on the door every time you crack open a bottle. Otherwise, you should feel free to tweak and embrace the flexible nature of this recipe. Fresh turmeric is a lovely substitute for dried\\u2014use about 3 tablespoons coarsely chopped or grated. And instead of dried hot chiles, use sliced fresh jalape\\u00f1o or habanero, or even smoke-dried ones. Consider adding other citrus, such as grapefruit or blood oranges, in place of or in addition to the lemon. Note: this recipe needs to sit for 1 month before enjoying.", "recipeYield": "Makes about 2 cups", "dateModified": "2017-02-23T16:53:50.085-05:00", "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/58af3b41d011dc426027376b/1:1/w_1126,h_1126,c_limit/Fire-Cider-hero-17022017.jpg", "datePublished": "2017-02-23T16:53:50.085-05:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 4, "ratingValue": 4.4}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 cup coarsely grated peeled horseradish (about 4 ounces)", "1 small onion, coarsely chopped", "8 large garlic cloves, smashed", "1/2 cup peeled and coarsely grated or chopped ginger (about 3 ounces)", "1 tablespoon ground turmeric", "1 teaspoon black peppercorns", "4 rosemary sprigs", "1 whole clove", "1\\u20132 dried hot chiles", "1 lemon, quartered", "2 cups (or more) unfiltered apple cider vinegar", "2 tablespoons (or more) honey", "A (preferably glass) quart container; cheesecloth", "Fire cider can be made 3 months ahead; store chilled in a (preferably glass) resealable container."], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Place horseradish, onion, garlic, ginger, turmeric, peppercorns, rosemary, and clove in quart jar. Crumble chile (use 2 if you like it spicy) into jar. Squeeze in lemon quarters; add rinds. Pour vinegar into jar until solids are fully submerged. Cover tightly, then swirl jar gently to combine. Let stand in a dark spot 1 month.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Strain through a cheesecloth-lined colander or sieve into a large measuring cup; discard solids. Gather up corners of cheesecloth to extract as much liquid as possible (wear gloves if you wish to avoid turmeric stains on your hands). Rinse out jar and pour in liquid. Add 2 Tbsp. honey, then shake covered jar or whisk to combine. Add more honey to taste.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "You can transfer mixture to a few smaller bottles, such as swing-top bottles, as it\\u2019s easier to pour from this way. Tightly seal and chill.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Cold Preventative:\\nSip by the spoonful when you feel a cold coming. You can also dilute it in water.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Fire Cider Tonic:\\nThis makes a great mocktail. Add about 1 Tbsp. fire cider and a squeeze of fresh orange juice to a glass of seltzer. Garnish with rosemary sprig.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Salad Dressing:\\nUse in place of apple cider vinegar in your favorite vinaigrette. You likely won\\u2019t need to add any additional sweetener.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Fire Cider Tea:\\nAdd about 1 Tbsp. fire cider to a mug of hot water, along with a squeeze of fresh lemon juice and a little honey to sweeten. Finish with a bit of freshly ground black pepper.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Fresh Herb Sauces:\\nUse fire cider in place of the red wine vinegar in sauces like chimichurri.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Marinade for fish, chicken, or tofu:\\nThink of fire cider as the acid in bright, assertive marinades similar to those for jerk chicken.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "While most recipes for fire cider use a heavy hand with the garlic because of its potent medicinal properties, we recommend going easy unless you want neighbors knocking on the door every time you crack open a bottle. Otherwise, you should feel free to tweak and embrace the flexible nature of this recipe. Fresh turmeric is a lovely substitute for dried\\u2014use about 3 tablespoons coarsely chopped or grated. And instead of dried hot chiles, use sliced fresh jalape\\u00f1o or habanero, or even smoke-dried ones. Consider adding other citrus, such as grapefruit or blood oranges, in place of or in addition to the lemon. Note: this recipe needs to sit for 1 month before enjoying.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:28:29.782932+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:40.511328+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:59.279447+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38705, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/pimms-royale-punch-56389839', 'epicurious', 'Pimm''s Royale Punch', 'Julie Reiner', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/55ac433e2165ea177986f6ff/master/w_2138,h_1425,c_limit/EP_07132015_summer100_pimsroyalepunch_6x4.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/pimms-royale-punch-56389839", "name": "Pimm''s Royale Punch", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/55ac433e2165ea177986f6ff/master/w_2138,h_1425,c_limit/EP_07132015_summer100_pimsroyalepunch_6x4.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Julie Reiner", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/julie-reiner"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Pimm''s Royale Punch", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["punch", "champagne", "pimm''s", "british", "cucumber", "grapefruit", "orange", "lemon", "strawberry", "beverages", "make ahead", "easter", "cookbooks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "Who says that Pimm''s is just for Pimm''s Cups? Add Champagne, and it becomes an especially refreshing punch. Pimm''s was created in the 1840s by an English oyster bar owner, and it became one of the most popular beverages in England. The exact recipe is a secret, but we do know that it is a gin-based liqueur flavored with spices and fruit. It is generally consumed in the Pimm''s Cup with ginger ale and a fancy fruit garnish. This party punch takes it one step farther, letting it macerate with fruit and then adding Champagne rather than soda.", "description": "Who says that Pimm''s is just for Pimm''s Cups? Add Champagne, and it becomes an especially refreshing punch. Pimm''s was created in the 1840s by an English oyster bar owner, and it became one of the most popular beverages in England. The exact recipe is a secret, but we do know that it is a gin-based liqueur flavored with spices and fruit. It is generally consumed in the Pimm''s Cup with ginger ale and a fancy fruit garnish. This party punch takes it one step farther, letting it macerate with fruit and then adding Champagne rather than soda.", "recipeYield": "Makes 15 servings", "dateModified": "2015-07-21T00:00:00.000-04:00", "datePublished": "2015-07-21T00:00:00.000-04:00", "recipeIngredient": ["Peels of 2 lemons, plus 2 lemons sliced into wheels", "\\u00bc cup granulated sugar", "1\\u00bd cups thinly sliced cucumber wheels", "\\u00bd grapefruit, sliced into wheels", "1 orange, sliced into wheels", "16 ounces Pimm''s No. 1", "4 ounces orange juice", "2 ounces lemon juice", "1 (750-ml) bottle Champagne", "Large ice block (optional)", "6 strawberries, hulled and sliced"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Place the peels in a glass pitcher or bowl with the sugar (save the lemons for juicing). Muddle the peels until the sugar looks slightly moistened, then cover and let sit for at least 1 hour, or overnight.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add the lemon, cucumber, grapefruit, and orange wheels, Pimm''s, orange juice, and lemon juice. Stir until the sugar has completely dissolved and refrigerate for at least 3 hours. You can make this the night before to cut your workload down on New Year''s Eve.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "When you are ready to serve, transfer the mixture (including the fruit) to a punch bowl and slowly add the Champagne and the ice. Garnish the bowl with the strawberry slices.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "To serve, ladle into punch glasses.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "This punch can also be served Sangria-style in a pitcher and poured over ice.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Who says that Pimm''s is just for Pimm''s Cups? Add Champagne, and it becomes an especially refreshing punch. Pimm''s was created in the 1840s by an English oyster bar owner, and it became one of the most popular beverages in England. The exact recipe is a secret, but we do know that it is a gin-based liqueur flavored with spices and fruit. It is generally consumed in the Pimm''s Cup with ginger ale and a fancy fruit garnish. This party punch takes it one step farther, letting it macerate with fruit and then adding Champagne rather than soda.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:50:59.644354+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:42.723464+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:25.187973+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (38781, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/bloody-hell-bloody-mary-51225810', 'epicurious', 'Bloody Hell Bloody Mary', 'Theresa Gilliam', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/555cd401644d45515b758ba4/master/w_2000,h_1334,c_limit/51225810_bloody-hell-bloody-mary_6x4.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/bloody-hell-bloody-mary-51225810", "name": "Bloody Hell Bloody Mary", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/555cd401644d45515b758ba4/master/w_2000,h_1334,c_limit/51225810_bloody-hell-bloody-mary_6x4.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Theresa Gilliam", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": "https://www.epicurious.com/contributor/theresa-gilliam"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Bloody Hell Bloody Mary", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["cocktail", "pitcher drink", "bloody mary", "beverages", "brunch", "nut free", "dairy free", "gluten free", "cookbooks", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "articleBody": "There are multiple stories around about who created the original bacon Bloody Mary. The battles about who was first or what drink is best have been contentious and slightly sordid. This version is a total bacon bust that includes bacon vodka, Bacon Salt\\u2122, and a bacon twist garnish. IT is so flavorful, you theoretically don''t even need to add the booze\\u2014but in all honesty, the booze-less variety has yet to be tested. J&D''s Bacon Salt is available online or at specialty food stores. If necessary, bacon flavored vodka, such as Bakon\\u2122 can be special ordered at your local liquor store.", "description": "There are multiple stories around about who created the original bacon Bloody Mary. The battles about who was first or what drink is best have been contentious and slightly sordid. This version is a total bacon bust that includes bacon vodka, Bacon Salt\\u2122, and a bacon twist garnish. IT is so flavorful, you theoretically don''t even need to add the booze\\u2014but in all honesty, the booze-less variety has yet to be tested. J&D''s Bacon Salt is available online or at specialty food stores. If necessary, bacon flavored vodka, such as Bakon\\u2122 can be special ordered at your local liquor store.", "recipeYield": "Makes about 3 cups", "dateModified": "2014-02-24T23:00:00.000-05:00", "datePublished": "2014-02-24T23:00:00.000-05:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 1, "ratingValue": 5}, "recipeIngredient": ["2 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce", "2 tablespoons freshly squeezed lemon juice", "1 teaspoon prepared horseradish", "1/2 teaspoon hot sauce, such as Tabasco brand", "1/4 teaspoon celery seed", "1/4 teaspoon ground coriander", "1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper", "1/4 teaspoon salt", "2 cups (16 ounces) tomato juice", "1/2-3/4 cup (4-6 ounces) bacon flavored vodka, or substitute plain", "2 tablespoons Bacon Salt, such as J&D''s brand", "Lime wedges", "Bacon Twists for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "In a large measuring cup or pitcher, combine the Worcestershire sauce, lemon juice, horseradish, hot sauce, celery seed, coriander, pepper, and salt. Add the tomato juice and vodka and stir well. Refrigerate until ready to serve.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Prepare 4 (8 ounce) drink glasses by rubbing the rim with a lime wedge and dipping in the Bacon Salt. Fill each glass with plenty of ice and divide the Bloody Mary mixture evenly among the glasses. Garnish each glass with a bacon twist and a lime wedge and serve immediately.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "There are multiple stories around about who created the original bacon Bloody Mary. The battles about who was first or what drink is best have been contentious and slightly sordid. This version is a total bacon bust that includes bacon vodka, Bacon Salt\\u2122, and a bacon twist garnish. IT is so flavorful, you theoretically don''t even need to add the booze\\u2014but in all honesty, the booze-less variety has yet to be tested. J&D''s Bacon Salt is available online or at specialty food stores. If necessary, bacon flavored vodka, such as Bakon\\u2122 can be special ordered at your local liquor store.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 22:01:50.659795+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:44.542536+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:48.162176+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39087, 'https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/spiced-milk-tea-masala-chai-355421', 'epicurious', 'Spiced Milk Tea (Masala Chai)', 'Epicurious', 'https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/579909083a12dd9d56024018/master/w_1000,h_662,c_limit/spiced-milk-tea-masala-chai.jpg',  E'{"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/spiced-milk-tea-masala-chai-355421", "name": "Spiced Milk Tea (Masala Chai)", "@type": "Recipe", "image": ["https://assets.epicurious.com/photos/579909083a12dd9d56024018/master/w_1000,h_662,c_limit/spiced-milk-tea-masala-chai.jpg"], "author": [{"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Person", "sameAs": ""}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "cookTime": "10 min", "headline": "Spiced Milk Tea (Masala Chai)", "isPartOf": {"name": "Epicurious", "@type": "CreativeWork"}, "keywords": ["hot drink", "black tea", "indian", "cardamom", "cinnamon", "beverages", "nonalcoholic", "gluten free", "nut free", "simmer", "ramadan", "gourmet", "web"], "publisher": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.epicurious.com/verso/static/epicurious-us/assets/logo-seo.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": "488px", "height": "100px"}, "name": "Epicurious", "@type": "Organization", "@context": "https://schema.org"}, "totalTime": "15 min", "articleBody": "Enjoyed by millions in India, masala chai, a spiced, sweetened black tea mixed with milk, is now popular around the world. It is sold all over India by chai wallahs, or tea vendors, who pour the tea from big kettles into small cups. Americans have incorrectly shortened the name to chai (which means simply \\"milk tea\\"); masala refers to the combination of spices, which often includes cardamom, cinnamon, ginger, cloves, pepper, fennel, and star anise. Although there are many chai blends available in supermarkets, making your own is quick and satisfying, and the results are much better.", "description": "Enjoyed by millions in India, masala chai, a spiced, sweetened black tea mixed with milk, is now popular around the world. It is sold all over India by chai wallahs, or tea vendors, who pour the tea from big kettles into small cups.", "dateModified": "2009-09-16T01:00:00.000-04:00", "datePublished": "2009-09-16T00:00:00.000-04:00", "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": 15, "ratingValue": 4.4}, "recipeIngredient": ["10 green cardamom pods, cracked, seeds removed, and pods discarded, or 1/2 teaspoon cardamom seeds or ground cardamom", "1 (1 1/2-inch) piece cinnamon stick", "4 peppercorns (preferably white)", "1/4 teaspoon fennel seeds", "2 cups whole milk", "3 1/2 tablespoons packed light brown sugar, or to taste", "1/2 teaspoon ground ginger", "2 cups water", "5 teaspoons loose orange pekoe tea or other black tea", "Equipment: a mortar and pestle or an electric coffee/spice grinder"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Grind together cardamom, cinnamon stick, peppercorns, and fennel seeds with mortar and pestle or coffee/spice grinder.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Bring milk just to a simmer in a 2-quart heavy saucepan. Stir or whisk in brown sugar, ground spice mixture, ginger, and 1/8 teaspoon salt, or to taste. Reduce heat to low and simmer gently, stirring occasionally, 3 minutes to infuse flavors.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Meanwhile, bring water to a boil in a 1-quart saucepan, add tea, and boil 1 minute.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Pour tea through a fine-mesh sieve into hot milk mixture (discard tea leaves) and cook over low heat 1 minute. Stir before serving.", "@type": "HowToStep"}], "alternativeHeadline": "Enjoyed by millions in India, masala chai, a spiced, sweetened black tea mixed with milk, is now popular around the world. It is sold all over India by chai wallahs, or tea vendors, who pour the tea from big kettles into small cups.", "isAccessibleForFree": true}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 22:02:50.674337+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:24:51.953968+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:48.162306+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39281, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/coconut-margarita-recipe-11726715', 'foodandwine', 'Coconut Margarita', 'Prairie Rose', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/ZjVoDb8sNF2C8tCNWPnVuUCm4WY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Coconut-Margarita-FT-RECIPE0525-56b4d535a6804584a55a050681d73087.jpeg',  E'{"name": "Coconut Margarita", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/ZjVoDb8sNF2C8tCNWPnVuUCm4WY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Coconut-Margarita-FT-RECIPE0525-56b4d535a6804584a55a050681d73087.jpeg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1000}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/prairie-rose-8606568", "name": "Prairie Rose", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Coconut Margarita", "prepTime": "PT1440M", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "4332 kcal", "fatContent": "198 g", "fiberContent": "21 g", "sugarContent": "258 g", "sodiumContent": "760 mg", "proteinContent": "21 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "297 g", "saturatedFatContent": "180 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT3M", "description": "This decadent Margarita variation from Los Angeles restaurant M\\u00edrate is made with coconut-washed reposado tequila, coconut cream, coconut liqueur, and fresh lime juice. Beverage director Maxwell Reis created it as a tribute to El Cholo, L.A.\\u2019s first Mexican restaurant.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2025-06-19T08:03:00-04:00", "datePublished": "2025-05-03T14:00:00-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American", "Mexican"], "recipeCategory": ["Appetizer", "Cocktail"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/coconut-margarita-recipe-11726715", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/tequila-cocktails-7496742", "name": "Tequila Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails-spirits/margaritas", "name": "Margaritas"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 cup of unsweetened coconut flakes", "1 bottle (750 ml) reposado tequila", "1 can (15 ounces) of Coco Lopez coconut cream", "1 can (11.25 ounces) condensed coconut milk\\u00a0", "1/2 bottle (16 ounces) coconut water (recommended brand: Harmless Harvest)", "1.5 ounces Toasted Coconut Washed Tequila*", ".5 ounces Kalani Coconut Liqueur", ".75 ounces M\\u00edrate Coconut Cr\\u00e8me**", ".75 ounces lime juice, freshly squeezed", "Toasted coconut flakes, for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"name": "Make the toasted coconut\\u2013washed tequila", "@type": "HowToSection", "itemListElement": [{"text": "Toast coconut flakes in a dry pan until golden.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Add flakes to a Ziplock bag with the bottle of tequila and sous vide at 145\\u00b0F for one hour (this can also be done in a pot with heated water and a thermometer).", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Move to a sealed storage container and freeze (retaining flakes) overnight.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Once defrosted, strain out flakes through a fine mesh metal strainer. (This may have to be done multiple times.)", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}, {"name": "Make the M\\u00edrate coconut cream", "@type": "HowToSection", "itemListElement": [{"text": "Warm cans of coconut cream and condensed coconut milk in a large container with warm water.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "In another container, combine all ingredients and immersion blend until smooth.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Store in the refrigerator and keep up to one month. Approx. 20 servings.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}, {"name": "Make the cocktail", "@type": "HowToSection", "itemListElement": [{"text": "Add all ingredients into an ice-filled shaker and shake until well-chilled.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Strain into a rocks glass.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Top with pebble ice.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Garnish with toasted coconut flakes.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:51:34.767949+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:00.128482+00:00'::timestamptz, 'Coconut Margarita', 'alias', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:16:50.806838+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39296, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/recipes/new-york-sour', 'foodandwine', 'New York Sour', 'Jodie Kautzmann', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/RDyg1jpOw1nzhx1O5HGFeIlw5sc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/new-york-sour-FT-RECIPE0321-eec62dfdf2774491827bb1138a61f5cf.jpg',  E'{"name": "New York Sour", "@type": ["Recipe", "NewsArticle"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/RDyg1jpOw1nzhx1O5HGFeIlw5sc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/new-york-sour-FT-RECIPE0321-eec62dfdf2774491827bb1138a61f5cf.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/jodie-kautzmann-7970407", "name": "Jodie Kautzmann", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "PoliteMolasses1534", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "I liked it! I don\\u2019t usually gravitate towards sours, but I was drawn to the pictures. I added an egg white which I will repeat next time. It was tangy and lightly sweet, and the zin made it jammy. The back of the spoon hack kept the layers separated.", "reviewRating": {"@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "4"}}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "Jackson", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "Smooth and very tasty. I one to find the perfect wine for this drink. Definitely a go to.", "reviewRating": {"@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "5"}, "datePublished": "2024-05-01T01:40:25.884Z"}, {"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "AmicableTablespoon8143", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "It was yummy. I was out of bourbon so I used rye. I had real maple syrup so I used that. And I had Meyer lemons so I used 1/2 of one. It was juicy enough. Pleased a drizzled the red wine gently enough to create the separate layer. It\\u2019s a pretty cocktail &amp; tasty.", "reviewRating": {"@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "4"}, "datePublished": "2024-04-07T01:44:16.881Z"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "New York Sour", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "200 kcal", "fatContent": "0 g", "fiberContent": "1 g", "sugarContent": "10 g", "sodiumContent": "1 mg", "proteinContent": "0 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "13 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT5M", "description": "The perfect balance of fruity red wine and smoky-sweet bourbon, the New York Sour cocktail is a classic for a reason.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2025-05-30T16:51:12-04:00", "datePublished": "2021-03-29T09:43:23-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Drink", "Beverage", "Cocktail"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "3", "ratingValue": "4.3"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/recipes/new-york-sour", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails-spirits", "name": "Spirits"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails-spirits/whisky", "name": "Whisky & Bourbon"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}]}}, "recipeIngredient": [".25 cup (2 ounces) bourbon", "2 tablespoons (1 ounce) fresh lemon juice (from 1 lemon)", "1 tablespoon (1/2 ounce) simple syrup", "2 tablespoons (1 ounce) fruity red wine, such as Zinfandel or Gamay", "1 stip lemon zest"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Gather the ingredients.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/CEOCUk77iQ0RmJbBCjhtrZdDjPA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/FAW-recipes-new-york-sour-step-01-6cbb8ba6fe46472c89a150bab11fddef.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "Fill a cocktail shaker with ice. Add bourbon, lemon juice, and simple syrup; seal lid on shaker and shake until chilled and frost forms on shaker, about 15 seconds. Strain into a rocks glass filled with large ice cubes.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/m74QpYT6w1qmATB7ktviQ4VM3Io=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/FAW-recipes-new-york-sour-step-02-c49cc21482714771bd804a3ce6d34e65.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "Gently and slowly, pour wine over the back of a spoon held just above the cocktail&#39;s surface, letting the wine float at top of glass.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/UK6CZFs6OnHqsND9Fa6_IS1IteI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/FAW-recipes-new-york-sour-step-03-ab59088cdfe04db1b0fb2f8d6265560e.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}, {"text": "Pinch lemon peel over the cocktail and run it around the rim of the glass; add peel to glass as a garnish. Serve immediately. This recipe was developed by Jasmine Smith; the text was written by Jodie Kautzmann.", "@type": "HowToStep", "image": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/cKTxS8g2BiY2jZ6Dv74uea3O-rg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/FAW-recipes-new-york-sour-step-04-db64752d3601425db10720aa50404b4d.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject"}]}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:51:36.679067+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:01.030405+00:00'::timestamptz, 'New York Sour', 'alias', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:16.950432+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39367, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/spiced-pear-spritz-recipe-6422212', 'foodandwine', 'Spiced Pear Spritz', 'Prairie Rose', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/BgeR-WkR1y9Kad30bsHSv_r6GjU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Spiced-Pear-Spritz-FT-RECIPE0120-4cf6faeef08c41f1a807c70037195b01.jpg',  E'{"name": "Spiced Pear Spritz", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/BgeR-WkR1y9Kad30bsHSv_r6GjU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Spiced-Pear-Spritz-FT-RECIPE0120-4cf6faeef08c41f1a807c70037195b01.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1000}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/prairie-rose-8606568", "name": "Prairie Rose", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Spiced Pear Spritz", "prepTime": "PT2M", "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT3M", "description": "The Spiced Pear Spritz is a fragrant cocktail made with pear vodka, falernum liqueur, Peychaud\\u2019s bitters, sparkling wine, and club soda. The uniquely tang of fresh pears combines with lime, clove, ginger notes, and bubbles.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2025-01-08T12:01:00-05:00", "datePublished": "2019-12-30T10:13:32-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Drink", "Appetizer", "Beverage"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/spiced-pear-spritz-recipe-6422212", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/vodka-cocktails-7496738", "name": "Vodka Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["2 tablespoons (1 ounce) pear-flavored vodka (such as Grey Goose La Poire)", "1 tablespoon (1/2 ounce) Velvet Falernum liqueur or simple syrup", "2 dashes Peychaud\\u2019s bitters", "4 to 6 tablespoons (2 to 3 ounces) chilled dry sparkling white wine", "Splash of club soda (optional)", "1 whole star anise"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "In a large, ice-filled wine glass add vodka, velvet falernum, and bitters.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Top with sparkling wine and a splash of club soda.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Garnish with star anise and a few pear slices.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:51:43.225758+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:04.855608+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:48.162306+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39508, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/sparkling-pear-punch-8363525', 'foodandwine', 'With Pears 5 Ways, This Punch Is a Celebration of Our Favorite Fall Orchard Fruit', 'M. Carrie Allan', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/rdfZBMtTbjM3oBt8J-dDTysOUyU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Sparkling-Pear-Punch-FT-RECIPE1223-738205e2c39f43f180e40761bb162832.jpg',  E'{"name": "With Pears 5 Ways, This Punch Is a Celebration of Our Favorite Fall Orchard Fruit", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/rdfZBMtTbjM3oBt8J-dDTysOUyU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Sparkling-Pear-Punch-FT-RECIPE1223-738205e2c39f43f180e40761bb162832.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1000}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/author/m-carrie-allan", "name": "M. Carrie Allan", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "With Pears 5 Ways, This Punch Is a Celebration of Our Favorite Fall Orchard Fruit", "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT10M", "description": "This effervescent pear punch celebrates fall and winter when pears are at their peak with the orchard fruit five ways \\u2014 pear brandy, floral pear nectar, perry (pear hard cider), and a garnish of sliced pears.", "recipeYield": "20 drinks", "dateModified": "2023-12-01T07:28:49-05:00", "datePublished": "2023-12-01T07:28:49-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Cocktail"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/sparkling-pear-punch-8363525", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["4 cups (32 ounces) pear brandy", "4 cups pear nectar", "2 cups (16 ounces) spiced pear liqueur (such as St. George) (see Note)", "1 cup fresh lemon juice (from about 5 lemons)", "1/2 cup (4 ounces) Licor 43", "1/2 teaspoon Angostura bitters", "3 cups (24 ounces) perry (pear hard cider) (such as Angry Orchard)", "Ice ring, for serving", "Pear slices, lemon wheels, whole star anise, and rosemary sprigs, for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Stir together pear brandy, nectar, liqueur, lemon juice, Licor 43, and bitters in a large punch bowl. Add hard cider; stir well to combine. Serve with ice ring and garnishes.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:51:57.312551+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:11.298931+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:56.834169+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39509, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/high-and-dry-cocktail-recipe-8350581', 'foodandwine', 'Sparkling Elderflower Negroni', 'Kaitlyn Stewart', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/zjv5sGi6GFud235Aafn82J5zsFY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/High-and-Dry-XL-RECIPE1123-b840fdcb91a547d5add4690cf6520012.jpg',  E'{"name": "Sparkling Elderflower Negroni", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/zjv5sGi6GFud235Aafn82J5zsFY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/High-and-Dry-XL-RECIPE1123-b840fdcb91a547d5add4690cf6520012.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1500}, "video": {"name": "How to Make a High and Dry Cocktail", "@type": "VideoObject", "duration": "PT27S", "contentUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/1CIIbYu2-b5wQURW0.mp4", "uploadDate": "2023-11-27T11:20:09-05:00", "description": "Unleash the tantalizing taste of sophistication with our video guide on how to make a High and Dry cocktail. Join us in the mixology realm as we craft this exquisite libation that blends premium spirits with a symphony of elevated flavors. From the first sip to the last drop, this cocktail promises a journey of refined indulgence.", "thumbnailUrl": "https://cdn.jwplayer.com/v2/media/1CIIbYu2/thumbnails/8gzr4gTn.jpg?width=1280"}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/kaitlyn-stewart-8362666", "name": "Kaitlyn Stewart", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Sparkling Elderflower Negroni", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "2415 kcal", "fatContent": "2 g", "fiberContent": "17 g", "sugarContent": "209 g", "sodiumContent": "45 mg", "proteinContent": "9 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "276 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT50M", "description": "The Sparkling Elderflower Negroni batched cocktail recipe combines gin, Campari, orange blossom water, elderflower liqueur, and dry sparkling wine. It&#39;s bittersweet, delicious, and can be made ahead and topped off with the sparkling wine upon serving at a party.", "recipeYield": "8 drinks", "dateModified": "2023-11-29T10:56:09-05:00", "datePublished": "2023-10-19T17:26:04-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Cocktail"], "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/high-and-dry-cocktail-recipe-8350581", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/gin-cocktails-7496744", "name": "Gin Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a03/4\\u00a0 \\u00a0 cup (6 ounces) Campari", "\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a03/4\\u00a0 \\u00a0 cup (6 ounces) elderflower liqueur (such as St-Germain)", "\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a03/4 \\u00a0 \\u00a0 cup (6 ounces) gin (such as Tanqueray)", "\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a01\\u00a0 \\u00a0 tsp. orange blossom water (such as Cortas)", "\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a02\\u00a0 \\u00a0 cups (16 oz.) dry sparkling wine", "\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0Grapefruit slices, for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Combine Campari, elderflower liqueur, gin, and orange blossom water in a serving pitcher. Stir well, about 15 seconds. Refrigerate until well chilled, about 45 minutes.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Remove Campari mixture from refrigerator; stir to recombine. Divide Campari mixture evenly among eight ice-filled wine glasses. Top each glass with 1/4 cup dry sparkling wine; garnish with a grapefruit slice.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:51:57.321384+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:11.341710+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:46.569254+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39523, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/recipes/orange-liqueur-mimosa', 'foodandwine', 'Orange Liqueur Mimosa', 'Liz Mervosh', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/Qz-M9d28u5V5QJmfli21eDKsNAY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/food-and-wine-mimosa-FT-RECIPE2019-0781f547a02e409497c00dfa10a9583e.jpg',  E'{"name": "Orange Liqueur Mimosa", "@type": ["Recipe", "NewsArticle"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/Qz-M9d28u5V5QJmfli21eDKsNAY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/food-and-wine-mimosa-FT-RECIPE2019-0781f547a02e409497c00dfa10a9583e.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1125}, "author": [{"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/author/liz-mervosh", "name": "Liz Mervosh", "@type": "Person"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Orange Liqueur Mimosa", "keywords": "cointreau", "nutrition": {"@type": "NutritionInformation", "calories": "1002 kcal", "fatContent": "1 g", "fiberContent": "1 g", "sugarContent": "175 g", "sodiumContent": "22 mg", "proteinContent": "2 g", "cholesterolContent": "0 mg", "carbohydrateContent": "188 g", "saturatedFatContent": "0 g", "unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"}, "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT75M", "description": "This Mimosa recipe swaps out traditional orange juice for homemade orange syrup and orange liqueur. Serve it at your next brunch or special occasion.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2023-10-11T17:07:43-04:00", "datePublished": "2021-12-30T11:00:44-05:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Drink", "Cocktail"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "1", "ratingValue": "5"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/recipes/orange-liqueur-mimosa", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails-spirits/brunch-cocktails", "name": "Brunch Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/sparkling-wine-cocktails-7496747", "name": "Sparkling Wine Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 cup fresh orange juice (from 4 [9-ounce] oranges), strained and pulp discarded", ".75 cup granulated sugar", "1 teaspoon orange liqueur (such as Grand Marnier)", ".75 cup (12 ounces) chilled sparkling wine (preferably Cava or Champagne)", "1 \\u00a0(2 1/2- x 1-inch) orange peel strip"], "recipeInstructions": [{"text": "Bring juice and sugar to a simmer in a small saucepan over medium, stirring occasionally. Reduce heat to low and simmer gently, stirring often, until sugar dissolves and mixture is slightly thickened, about 2 minutes. Remove from heat. Transfer orange syrup to a small jar or pitcher and chill uncovered until cold, about 1 hour, or refrigerate in an airtight container for up to 3 weeks.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Prepare the Mimosa: Pour orange liqueur and 1 1/2 teaspoons orange syrup into a tulip-style Champagne glass (or a white wine glass). Tilt glass slightly, and slowly pour sparkling wine into glass. Holding orange peel strip in 1 hand, squeeze and rub peel sides together over the glass to release essential oils. Gently drop peel into glass. Serve immediately.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:52:01.873932+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:11.958824+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:20.960757+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
insert into public.recipes (id, source_url, site, name, author, image_url, jsonld, fetched_at, extracted_at, canonical_name, canonical_name_source, normalizer_version, normalized_at, cluster_id, variant_key, dedup_version) values (39529, 'https://www.foodandwine.com/the-retropolitan-cocktail-7972682', 'foodandwine', 'Strawberry-Infused Aperol Is My New Favorite Party Trick', 'The Betty at the Kimpton Sylvan Hotel, Atlanta', 'https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/cKn5iFkb51om9EaTFrrAM4f_pLM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/The-Retropolitan-XL-RECIPE1023-d9e8f494022c4e6494d890cc47ec8c44.jpg',  E'{"name": "Strawberry-Infused Aperol Is My New Favorite Party Trick", "@type": ["Recipe"], "image": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/cKn5iFkb51om9EaTFrrAM4f_pLM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/The-Retropolitan-XL-RECIPE1023-d9e8f494022c4e6494d890cc47ec8c44.jpg", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 1500, "height": 1500}, "author": [{"name": "The Betty at the Kimpton Sylvan Hotel, Atlanta", "@type": "Person"}], "review": [{"@type": "Review", "author": {"name": "test", "@type": "Person"}, "reviewBody": "\\"&gt;", "reviewRating": {"@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "1"}, "datePublished": "2023-11-14T09:15:20.310Z"}], "@context": "http://schema.org", "headline": "Strawberry-Infused Aperol Is My New Favorite Party Trick", "publisher": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com", "logo": {"url": "https://www.foodandwine.com/thmb/uV0O06O8WNrLepjgxkntdVuRpeE=/112x112/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/brand_logo_schema-f3b2e548eb6f4243ad527798593483e0.png", "@type": "ImageObject", "width": 112, "height": 112}, "name": "Food & Wine", "@type": "Organization", "brand": "Food & Wine", "sameAs": ["https://www.facebook.com/foodandwine", "https://www.instagram.com/foodandwine/?hl=en", "https://www.pinterest.com/foodandwine/", "https://flipboard.com/@foodandwine", "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT1455M", "description": "A riff on a traditional Cosmopolitan cocktail calls for strawberry-infused Aperol instead of the cranberry juice in this sweet drink. Spoon the leftover liqueur-soaked strawberries over sorbet or ice cream for an additional treat.", "recipeYield": "1 drink", "dateModified": "2023-09-25T09:35:19-04:00", "datePublished": "2023-09-25T09:35:19-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Cocktail"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "1", "ratingValue": "1"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/the-retropolitan-cocktail-7972682", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/vodka-cocktails-7496738", "name": "Vodka Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 cup (8 ounces) Aperol", "1/2 cup ripe strawberries, stemmed and quartered", "3 tablespoons (1 1/2 ounces) vodka (such as Boyd &amp; Blair)", "2 tablespoons (1 ounce) strawberry-infused Aperol", "1 tablespoon (1/2 ounce) orange liqueur (such as Cointreau)", "1 tablespoon fresh lime juice", "1 teaspoon simple syrup", "Mint sprig and fresh strawberries, for garnish"], "recipeInstructions": [{"name": "Make the Retropolitan", "text": "Combine Aperol and strawberries in an airtight container, and refrigerate for 24 hours. Strain Aperol and set aside. Reserve liqueur-soaked strawberries for another use, if desired.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Combine vodka, strawberry-infused Aperol, orange liqueur, lime juice, and simple syrup in a cocktail shaker filled with ice. Place lid on shaker; shake until mixture is cold, about 15 seconds. Strain into a coupe glass. Garnish with a mint sprig and fresh strawberries.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:51:58.651721+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:12.152620+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:48.162306+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
