.com/channel/UCKH_4hkRSyUSHDIFMzlGCRA", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_%26_Wine"], "publishingPrinciples": "https://www.foodandwine.com/about-us-6373913#toc-editorial-policies"}, "totalTime": "PT10M", "description": "These mezcal Margaritas are made with Meyer lemons, ginger, and Makrut lime leaves for a complex, smoky, floral cocktail.", "recipeYield": "1", "dateModified": "2023-06-15T16:07:11-04:00", "datePublished": "2023-06-15T15:07:33-04:00", "recipeCuisine": ["American"], "recipeCategory": ["Cocktail"], "aggregateRating": {"@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingCount": "1", "ratingValue": "5"}, "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/meyer-lemon-mezcal-margarita-7547308", "@type": ["WebPage"], "breadcrumb": {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/drinks", "name": "Drinks"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails", "name": "Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/tequila-cocktails-7496742", "name": "Tequila Cocktails"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3}, {"item": {"@id": "https://www.foodandwine.com/cocktails-spirits/margaritas", "name": "Margaritas"}, "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4}]}}, "recipeIngredient": ["1 Makrut lime leaf", "2 tablespoons kosher salt", "1 tablespoons sugarMargarita", "1 Meyer lemon wedge", "2 ounces mezcal", "2 ounces Meyer lemon juice", "1 ounce simple syrup", "1 teaspoon finely grated ginger (from a 1-inch piece of ginger)", "1 Makrut lime leaf, crushed", "1 (1-inch) strip lemon zest"], "recipeInstructions": [{"name": "Make the Margarita", "text": "Heat lime leaf in a 350\\u00b0F oven for 2 minutes or in a microwave on High for 1 minute, until dried and crumbly. Place toasted lime leaf, salt, and sugar in a spice grinder and grind into a powder. Transfer to a rimmed plate.", "@type": "HowToStep"}, {"text": "Moisten rim of a large rocks glass with lemon wedge; dip edge of glass into Lime Leaf Salt. Combine mezcal, lemon juice, simple syrup and ginger in pint glass. Add ice and shake vigorously. Pour Margarita into salt-rimmed glass, garnish with lime leaf and lemon zest and serve.", "@type": "HowToStep"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-04-23 20:52:04.061879+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-04-25 19:25:14.671124+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, 'pending_llm', 'v1', '2026-05-03 23:17:10.797560+00:00'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, NULL);
